02/books/review-marina-abramovic-memoir-walk-through-walls.html', 'snippet': 'The performance artist, who had a popular 2010 retrospective at the Museum of Modern Art, implicitly bids readers to warm their hands on the blaze of her greatness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marina Abramovic’s first major performance art piece was based on an old Russian drinking game. In front of an audience in 1973, she took a series of sharp knives and stabbed each as quickly as she could into the spaces between her fingers. (In the game, there is only one knife and you take a drink for each nick.) Blood went everywhere.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 918}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/arts/02BOOKABRAMOVIC/02BOOKABRAMOVIC-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,