 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is a coherent theme to this year’s election, it is the growing economic frustration of working Americans. While trade has been the chief scapegoat, a major culprit has received much less attention: the rising cost of health insurance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Health Care Hurts Your Paycheck', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Health Care Hurts Your Paycheck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Regina E. Herzlinger, Barak D. Richman and Richard J. Boxer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Regina', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Herzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Barak', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe657e6-2b13-545c-bd83-4019c9dc7139', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe657e6-2b13-545c-bd83-4019c9dc7139'}, {'abstract': 'When is a cause worth courting chaos?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/opinion/campaign-stops/from-roe-to-trump.html', 'snippet': 'When is a cause worth courting chaos?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 22, 1973, the Supreme Court of the United States, by a 7-2 majority, discovered a sweeping constitutional rig