rapher who works in the sky shooting the ground below, the situation was literal. But Mr. Kowalski didn’t start flying to photograph — he photographed to fly, and he did so in order to fuel what he describes as an addiction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing Everyday Beauty From Above', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gliders, Hang Gliding and Paragliding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kowalski, Kacper', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T08:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcad5217-3630-5d5b-8d53-1f280c415a6c', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcad5217-3630-5d5b-8d53-1f280c415a6c'}, {'abstract': 'What do you think this image is saying? How does it relate to current events?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/learning/across-the-fence.html', 'snippet': 'What do you think this image is saying? How does it relate to current events?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is an illustration that went with a recent Op-Ed essay in The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/opinion/sunday/30orner/30orner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'arti