'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f4436ba-d91d-56e3-ba52-b36934705ba7', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f4436ba-d91d-56e3-ba52-b36934705ba7'}, {'abstract': 'If you want to be happy for the rest of your life, new books suggest working hard and playing nice; taking it a few steps at a time; watching your pocketbook; and just not trying so much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/books/review/how-to-be-happy.html', 'snippet': 'If you want to be happy for the rest of your life, new books suggest working hard and playing nice; taking it a few steps at a time; watching your pocketbook; and just not trying so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m a happy person. Here’s my secret: Every day I anticipate things will go horribly wrong, and when they don’t I am surprised, grateful and a little bit elated. For example, today I don’t have a brain tumor! My children can be obnoxious, but they’re not (as far as I know) plotting ways to trigger my life insurance policy! There’s always tomorrow, of course, but right now things look good. I’m the Queen of Low Expectations, and proud of it.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/books/review/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/books/review/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/books/review/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02/1106-BKS-HelpDesk-SUB02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, '