hursday, Nov. 10.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE7/06GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andreas Gursky’s Vibrant Photography at Gagosian', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Bold at a Distance, Detailed Up Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Not Abstract II (Exhibit)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gursky, Andreas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T17:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/713d6bd7-1f17-547a-a15d-109607ec52c4', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/713d6bd7-1f17-547a-a15d-109607ec52c4'}, {'abstract': 'In this adaptation of the movie “The Band’s Visit,” an Egyptian band that arrives in Israel ends up stranded in a remote village after a mix-up at the border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/theater/atlantic-theater-company-has-a-new-musical-from-david-yazbek.html', 'snippet': 'In this adaptation of the movie “The Band’s Visit,” an Egyptian band that arrives in Israel ends up stranded in a remote village after a mix-up at the border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2001, the composer and lyricist David Yazbek, who wrote for “Late Night With David Letterman” for a stint in the early 1980s, told a Toronto newspaper: “I’d always wondered if I could write a song that could get the kind of laughs that a good sketch could get.” His career in musical theater has made that possible, starting in 2000 with his delightful Broadway debut “The Full Monty,” a charming musical that was funnier than the 1997 movie. He has since worked in many mediums, including television and cabaret, but has written a new musical about every five years. His latest, which starts previews Off Broadway at the Atlantic Theater Company on Friday, Nov. 11, is another adaptation, this time of the movie “The Band’s Visit,” about an Egyptian group that arrives in Israel to play a show but ends up stranded in a remote village after a mix-up at the border. Itamar Moses wrote the book, and David Cromer, who replaced Hal Prince, directs a cast that includes John Cariani and Tony Shalhoub. (atlantictheater.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE8/06GUIDE8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlantic Theater Company Has a New Musical From David Yazbek', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; Border Trouble Strands a Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yazbek, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Band's Visit (Play)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalhoub, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T18:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21caad41-8130-5ac0-b84b-c59c127ebc57', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21caad41-8130-5ac0-b84b-c59c127ebc57'}, {'abstract': 'Jonah Bokaer’s choreography links each dancer to someone in the Italian dramatist Luigi Pirandello’s “Six Characters in Search of an Author.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/arts/dance/rules-of-the-game-a-multilayered-dance-is-coming-to-bam.html', 'snippet': 'Jonah Bokaer’s choreography links each dancer to someone in the Italian dramatist Luigi Pirandello’s “Six Characters in Search of an Author.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life can involve game upon game. Jonah Bokaer, a former member of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, relishes choreographic games. And “Rules of the Game,” his new dance production, is a puzzle of artistic layers. It takes its title from a work by the great Italian dramatist Luigi Pirandello, as well as another play that is being rehearsed by actors in Pirandello’s “Six Characters in Search of an Author,” who find themselves invaded by characters from still another, but unfinished, drama. Mr. Bokaer said that although his creation is plotless, his choreography subtly links each dancer to someone in “Six Characters.” It haunts the production, designed by Daniel Arsham (with new music by Pharrell Williams), with Pirandello ghosts. Mr. Bokaer’s program, which celebrates 10 years of collaborating with Mr. Arsham, also includes “Recess,” a solo, and — more games — “Why Patterns,” in which dancers interact with multitudes of table tennis balls. (Thursday, Nov. 10, through Saturday at 7:30 p.m., BAM Howard Gilman Opera House, Fort Greene; 718-636-4100, bam.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 503}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE6/06GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Rules of the Game,’ a Multilayered Dance, Is Coming to BAM', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; A Layered Puzzle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bokaer, Jonah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rules of the Game (Dance)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T18:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bf4d1d7-ed8e-5830-8b74-ff44118ebe13', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bf4d1d7-ed8e-5830-8b74-ff44118ebe13'}, {'abstract': 'Investments in sensor and radar technologies and increased staffing might be the best and most cost-efficient way to patrol America’s borders with Mexico and Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/03/us/drones-canadian-border.html', 'snippet': 'Investments in sensor and radar technologies and increased staffing might be the best and most cost-efficient way to patrol America’s borders with Mexico and Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRAND FORKS, N.D. — Cameras on drones stare down at the Canadian border from as high as 28,000 feet, scanning vast stretches of mountains, rivers and forests for potential terrorists and drug smugglers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/us/03drone1/03drone1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Drones, So Useful in War, May Be Too Costly for Border Duty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Though Useful in War, Drones May Be Too Costly for Use Along U.S. Borders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radar', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T18:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a6e9eeb-916d-53c0-834a-12c4cb1ad5d4', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a6e9eeb-916d-53c0-834a-12c4cb1ad5d4'}, {'abstract': 'These R&B stalwarts tap the emotional well as they bring their “King and Queen of Hearts Tour” to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/arts/music/mary-j-blige-and-maxwell-at-the-garden.html', 'snippet': 'These R&B stalwarts tap the emotional well as they bring their “King and Queen of Hearts Tour” to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Depending on the artist, when the personal bleeds aggressively into the professional, it can be a recipe for either messiness or motivation. For Mary J. Blige, the veteran R&B belter who’s at her best when emotionally charged, heartbreak is inspiration. This summer, she filed for divorce from her husband of more than a decade and longtime manager, but instead of cowering from tabloid headlines, she has worked them into her live show. A recent single, “Thick of It,” from her coming album “Strength of a Woman,” is similarly defiant: “Who’s gonna love you like I do? Who will you trust? I gave you too much.” That combination of vulnerability and resilience can be expected when Ms. Blige and Maxwell, the progressive soul seducer, headline Madison Square Garden on Thursday, Nov. 10, as part of their “King and Queen of Hearts Tour.” “I don’t hold back,” Ms. Blige said recently, “and there’s no way I am going to start changing now.” (ticketmaster.com)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1034, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1034}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 595, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE4/06GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary J. Blige and Maxwell at the Garden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; The Seducer and the Belter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blige, Mary J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maxwell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T18:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac96edcd-f183-57a4-8d00-7e7a96592d1a', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac96edcd-f183-57a4-8d00-7e7a96592d1a'}, {'abstract': 'An anti-Clinton tweet is just the latest example. This language reminds women of what we’ve been through.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/opinion/the-power-of-anti-hillary-slurs.html', 'snippet': 'An anti-Clinton tweet is just the latest example. This language reminds women of what we’ve been through.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One night, after the Democratic convention, I caught a train back to downtown Philadelphia. Some men boarded the train a few stops after me, shouting about Hillary Clinton. I took out my earphones to listen. “She’s a slut who belongs in jail,” one of them said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/opinion/2weds04/2weds04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Adviser’s Slur Is a Sign of Things to Come', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Alex (1974- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Sid (1955- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-02T18:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f6914a-47b1-5f18-a954-96215770e9b8', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f6914a-47b1-5f18-a954-96215770e9b8'}, {'abstract': 'Yael Stone plays a police detective investigating a vicious killing with sexual undercurrents in a suburb of Sydney, Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/arts/television/deep-water-a-crime-thriller-comes-to-acorn-tv.html', 'snippet': 'Yael Stone plays a police detective investigating a vicious killing with sexual undercurrents in a suburb of Sydney, Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of “Orange Is the New Black” know her as Lorna Morello, the hard-on-the-ears, sweetly delusional Litchfield Penitentiary inmate whose romantic travails have kept Netflix viewers in stitches for four seasons. But somewhere beneath Morello’s ruby-red lipstick, cockeyed accent and histrionics lurks the Australian actress Yael Stone. And in “Deep Water,” a crime thriller debuting Monday, Nov. 7, on Acorn TV, she’s virtually unrecognizable. Her face scrubbed bare and her vowels subdued, Ms. Stone plays Tori Lustigman, a police detective investigating a vicious killing with sexual undercurrents in a suburb of Sydney. But when a clue links the case to a similar one from 26 years earlier, Tori uncovers 70 possible murders of gay men spanning decades along New South Wales’s glorious shoreline — and the possibility that the culprit is back at it. “Every day, Tori, you come to work prepared to give up your life to protect others,” her boss says. “But you’ve got a son. Why would you do that?” Some secrets can’t be washed away.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE1/06GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Deep Water,’ a Crime Thriller, Comes to Acorn TV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Detectiv