11 Trilogy will be shown, and she will take questions after “The Oath” and “Citizenfour.” Also coming up: the Doc NYC festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/movies/laura-poitras-and-her-films-at-the-museum-of-the-moving-image.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Poitras’s so-called 9/11 Trilogy will be shown, and she will take questions after “The Oath” and “Citizenfour.” Also coming up: the Doc NYC festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the surreal election season about to end, documentaries move to the fore, starting at the Museum of the Moving Image in Queens with “Pushing the Envelope,” a program of nonfiction films that won or were nominated for Cinema Eye Honors. On Sunday, Nov. 6, Laura Poitras’s so-called 9/11 Trilogy will be shown. “My Country, My Country” follows an Iraqi physician who runs for office; “The Oath” introduces a Yemeni cabdriver who was once Osama bin Laden’s bodyguard, and his brother-in-law, a prisoner at Guantánamo. “Citizenfour,” of course, is her Academy Award-winning account of meeting with the former N.S.A. contractor Edward J. Snowden in Hong Kong. Ms. Poitras (and the cinematographer Kirsten Johnson) will take questions after “The Oath” and “Citizenfour.” (718-784-0077; movingimage.us)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE5/06GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE5/06GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/arts/06GUIDE5/06GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 