ia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2b4e3152-4d99-54c9-94af-d19e04c8fd5b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2b4e3152-4d99-54c9-94af-d19e04c8fd5b'}, {'abstract': 'Athi-Patra Ruga staged “Over the Rainbow” — and introduced his newest avatar, Versatile Queen Ivy — for Performa’s fall gala.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/t-magazine/art/athi-patra-ruga-over-the-rainbow-performa.html', 'snippet': 'Athi-Patra Ruga staged “Over the Rainbow” — and introduced his newest avatar, Versatile Queen Ivy — for Performa’s fall gala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Draped in billowing, Champagne-colored satin with a haphazard stack of tiaras strapped to his head, the artist Athi-Patra Ruga sprawled on a dance-studio floor in Brooklyn last Saturday, holding court. “There are so many South Africas, and that’s the story of South Africa,” he proclaimed to those listening, the director and chief curator of Performa RoseLee Goldberg among them. He then paused to collect his thoughts; in Ruga time, both a stray millisecond sans speech and a minute-long interruption for dramatic effect seem entirely intentional. “Maybe,” he determined, “I should start with the whole ‘rainbow’ thing.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/t-magazine/01tmag-performa-slide-NAY2/01tmag-performa-slide-NAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/01/t-magazine/01tmag-performa-slide-NAY2/01tmag-performa-slide-NAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/t-mag