presidency, only an independent investigation may save it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South Korea’s President Park Geun-hye is embroiled in a lurid corruption scandal that threatens to hamstring her remaining year in office. The scandal has plunged Ms. Park’s approval ratings to record lows, sent thousands of angry demonstrators into the streets, and sparked demands that she resign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea’s Metastasizing Crisis', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea’s Political Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Choi Soon-sil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-03T14:08:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fa72611-4f5c-5e30-b66d-58f6a5010937', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fa72611-4f5c-5e30-b66d-58f6a5010937'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The French forces at the Somme make a push toward Sailly-Saillisel and Lesboeufs and take 736 prisoners, in November 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/03/1916-french-push-on-north-of-somme-despite-downpour/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The French forces at the Somme make a push toward Sailly-Saillisel and Lesboeufs and take 736 prisoners, in November 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The persistence of the rain on the Somme front is seriously hindering infantry operations, but despite this the Allies continue to display a certain activity. During Wednesday night and yesterday [Nov. 2] the Fre