 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/42f30c81-ac44-507f-98e1-264bf52fcd3c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/42f30c81-ac44-507f-98e1-264bf52fcd3c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a country where men use misogyny to destroy their enemies — and get away with it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/04/opinion/what-locker-room-talk-sounds-like-in-the-philippines.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a country where men use misogyny to destroy their enemies — and get away with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Machismo isn’t quite what it used to be. Backlash and hashtags now hold politicians accountable for their so-called locker-room talk in much of the world. Yet the Philippines remains a glaring example of how men use language and law to try to emasculate opponents and maintain power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What ‘Locker-Room Talk’ Sounds Like in the Philippines', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Misogyny as weapon  in Manila', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duterte, Rodrigo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Estrada, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacquiao, Manny', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Lima, Leila (1959- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-03T15:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Syjuco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Syjuco', 'qualifier': No