y-hi-los-angeles-restaurant-miso-bowl-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Honey Hi combines the best of all the health food trends that have become synonymous with West Coast wellness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dietary dogma is so strong in Los Angeles that even Dodgers Stadium offers vegan and gluten-free options for fervent-but-sensitive gamegoers. And down the road at Honey Hi in Echo Park, Eastsiders are catching a new wave of nutrition. It’s not strictly vegetarian, vegan, paleo, raw, plant-based, ayurvedic or superfoodist. The restaurant’s guiding principle is what they call a radical inclusivity. But according to its co-owner Kacie Carter, a chef and nutritionist, Honey Hi isn’t a movement, it’s simply “a little cafe with delicious food that makes you feel good.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/t-magazine/food/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/03/t-magazine/food/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/t-magazine/food/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/03/t-magazine/food/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/03/t-magazine/food/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT/03tmag-honey-hi-slide-UGRT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 