le/25c42865-8b75-5972-8a90-501a6ae93fb5'}, {'abstract': 'A former editor in chief of The New England Journal of Medicine explains foreseeable negative consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/05/opinion/a-public-option-for-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'A former editor in chief of The New England Journal of Medicine explains foreseeable negative consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Public Option for Health Care', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Public Option for Health', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-04T17:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/090eeaea-e915-5700-8539-3cf8c711ff9f', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/090eeaea-e915-5700-8539-3cf8c711ff9f'}, {'abstract': 'For the 33-year-old waitress, athlete and single mother, running comes first (before the sun rises) so she can fit in as many hours as possible with her daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/nyregion/how-domenica-ramos-marathon-runner-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'For the 33-year-old waitress, athlete and single mother, running comes first (before the sun rises) so she can fit in as many hours as possible with her daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Domenica Ramos immigrated to New York City from Ecuador in 2001. In 2013, she started starting running to cope with the stress of single motherhood and quickly became a Boston Marathon qualifier, finishing her fourth marathon last month in Chicago with a time of 3 hours 24 minutes 12 seconds. A resident of Hamilton Heights in Manhattan, Ms. Ramos, 33, balances training with 12-hour waitressing shifts and caring for her 6-year-old daughter, Gabriela. She was hoping to finish the New York City Marathon in 3 hours 20 minutes. Recently, however, a mild injury flared up, threatening to slow Ms. Ramos down, but not stop her: “Deeply in my heart,” she said, “I want to line up at the start and run this marathon.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE1/06ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Domenica Ramos, Marathon Runner, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Runner Keeps Pace for Her ‘Little Coach’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crouse, Lindsay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chicago Marathon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamilton Heights (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Domenica', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-04T17:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5bac0de-34d0-5cf3-83b9-4c95432ed964', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5bac0de-34d0-5cf3-83b9-4c95432ed964'}, {'abstract': 'Work celebrations are a tradition in Hollywood. With “Office Christmas Party” coming out, here are some other film and TV bashes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/movies/office-christmas-party-and-holiday-parties-onscreen.html', 'snippet': 'Work celebrations are a tradition in Hollywood. With “Office Christmas Party” coming out, here are some other film and TV bashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the typical corporate holiday affair, co-workers might let their hair