nyt://article/0da058ae-6805-56ce-b1a7-f6c7b3176456'}, {'abstract': 'What a World Series — especially if you’ve played for both the Cubs and Terry Francona.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/05/opinion/united-loyalties.html', 'snippet': 'What a World Series — especially if you’ve played for both the Cubs and Terry Francona.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a baseball analyst for ESPN, I have to remain neutral, but that doesn’t erase my history. I was a Chicago Cub, and I also played for Terry Francona, now the Cleveland Indians manager, what seems like a lifetime ago. So amid the excitement of seeing my first professional organization have a chance to win it all, and get further than I ever reached in my major-league career, I knew that someone had to lose. And I had friends on both sides.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05glanvilleWeb/05glanvilleWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05glanvilleWeb/05glanvilleWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05glanvilleWeb/05glanvilleWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05glanvilleWeb/05glanvilleWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05glanvilleWeb/05glanvilleWeb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard'