on, the federal Education Department announced that the city agreed to revamp its procedures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public schools are required to educate children with disabilities in regular classrooms as much as possible, but according to a federal investigation, the Yonkers school system routinely flouted that rule. And instead of creating a specific plan for each student, as is required, the district essentially copied and pasted language from one child’s file to the next.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yonkers Schools Flouted Rules on Special Education, U.S. Agency Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Agency Says Yonkers Flouted Rules on Special Ed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yonkers (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-05T00:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0171ad1d-5afe-5bd2-b5c9-d6de9255df52', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0171ad1d-5afe-5bd2-b5c9-d6de9255df52'}, {'abstract': 'As the region has become more congested and expensive, there are growing demands to rein in the physical space that many technologists call home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/05/technology/silicon-valley-california-growth.html', 'snippet': 'As the region has become more congested and expensive, there are growing demands to rein in the physical space that many technologists call home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CUPERTINO, Calif. — Silicon Valley is bent on disrupting the world. Its products affect how millions upon millions of people live and work. But when it comes to the physical space that many technologists call home, there are increasing demands to leave things alone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/us/05VALLEY/05VALLEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width':