', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ad03439-5c93-5a7a-9174-2cf17eabfaf5'}, {'abstract': 'In Iowa and Florida, it’s actually been Republican supporters accused of fraud. Yet their party continues to try to disenfranchise minority voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/05/opinion/republicans-and-the-myth-of-election-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'In Iowa and Florida, it’s actually been Republican supporters accused of fraud. Yet their party continues to try to disenfranchise minority voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years Republicans in state legislatures have expressed grave concern about voter fraud as they presented a “solution” of tough voter ID laws and other restrictions that deprive low-income and minority voters of the ballot. Many of these voter-suppression measures have become law despite clear evidence that voter fraud is practically nonexistent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05barberWeb/05barberWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05barberWeb/05barberWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05barberWeb/05barberWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05barberWeb/05barberWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/05/opinion/05barberWeb/05barberWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width':