 Axtell became police chief in St. Paul, he happened to meet Frank Baker, a local resident who wished him well in his new job. Then, the next night, a police dog bit Mr. Baker on the leg and a police officer kicked him, leaving him hospitalized for two weeks with collapsed lungs and large lacerations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Violent Encounter Between Police and a Black Man, Something Rare — An Apology', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Police Used Force on Minnesota Man, Something Rare Followed: An Apology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Paul (Minn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Frank (1963- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Axtell, Todd D (1968- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-05T02:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96306b4c-b433-576b-a675-387d5f3aca8d', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96306b4c-b433-576b-a675-387d5f3aca8d'}, {'abstract': 'A town that hosted thousands of travelers after Sept. 11 is the subject of a musical opening this month in Toronto. Plus, revelations that the police spied on journalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/05/world/canada/canada-today.html', 'snippet': 'A town that hosted thousands of travelers after Sept. 11 is the subject of a musical opening this month in Toronto. Plus, revelations that the police spied on journalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When terrorist attacks grounded air travel on Sept. 11, 2001, Gander, Newfoundland, population 11,000, found itself playing host to 6,700 stranded travelers, most of them American. While that made the town famous for hospitality worldwide, its residents tend to play down their contributions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/arts/05canadatoday/01GANDER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi