, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e28879-8813-5a5a-825a-8208916f6e3f', 'word_count': 1655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e28879-8813-5a5a-825a-8208916f6e3f'}, {'abstract': 'Justices revived a state law that bans people from collecting other voters’ completed absentee ballots and submitting them to election officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/06/us/politics/arizona-supreme-court-absentee-ballots.html', 'snippet': 'Justices revived a state law that bans people from collecting other voters’ completed absentee ballots and submitting them to election officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court issued an order on Saturday allowing Arizona to enforce a law banning so-called ballot harvesting, in which others collect voters’ completed absentee ballots and submit them to election officials. The court’s two-sentence order stayed a ruling from the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit that would have temporarily blocked the law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona Can Ban ‘Ballot Harvesting,’ Supreme Court Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Lets Arizona Ban ‘Harvesting’ of Ballots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Absentee Voting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-05T17:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Nationa