_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Risk to Civil Liberties of Fighting Crime With Big Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Risks to Civil Liberties When Big Data Is Put to Work Fighting Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (Chicago, Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reed Elsevier NV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RELX Group', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-06T23:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d4cdd2-c363-518b-8923-243749ebd645', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d4cdd2-c363-518b-8923-243749ebd645'}, {'abstract': 'Hillary Clinton’s aides, helped by data models and experience in the elections of 2008 and 2012, have long shifted their focus away from the “Bubba” voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/07/us/politics/bill-clinton-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Hillary Clinton’s aides, helped by data models and experience in the elections of 2008 and 2012, have long shifted their focus away from the “Bubba” voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PUEBLO, Colo. — After obliging a request for a selfie from a woman in the lobby, Bill Clinton left his hotel here on Friday and rode to his rally, where he made the case that Hillary Clinton cared more about restoring jobs to forgotten workers than Donald J. Trump did.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/07/us/07billclinton3/07billclinton3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bi