me': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/e62874c0-9264-55ef-9ba1-d5af292a8970', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62874c0-9264-55ef-9ba1-d5af292a8970'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court turned away a bid to reinstate a trial judge’s order that barred Donald J. Trump’s campaign from harassing or intimidating voters in Ohio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/08/us/politics/supreme-court-donald-trump-ohio.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court turned away a bid to reinstate a trial judge’s order that barred Donald J. Trump’s campaign from harassing or intimidating voters in Ohio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday refused to intercede in a lawsuit brought by the Ohio Democratic Party against Donald J. Trump’s presidential campaign. The justices turned away a last-minute bid from the party to reinstate a sweeping order from a trial judge that had barred the Trump campaign from harassing or intimidating voters in Ohio.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08scotus/08scotus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08scotus/08scotus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08scotus/08scotus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08scotus/08scotus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width':