on their livestock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Mude, a Kenyan economist, has a way of explaining satellites. When he’s talking to pastoralists in his country’s north — people who roam the earth with a dozen head of cattle and very little else — he talks about the stars that don’t act like other stars. “They’re actually taking pictures of the ground,” Mude says. Herders, a stargazing people, understand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Up in the Sky, Help to Keep Africans From Starving', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shariah (Islamic Law)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nomadic People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Livestock Research Institute', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T08:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b864472b-453f-5252-a234-b7ae1d72022c', 'word_count': 1611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b864472b-453f-5252-a234-b7ae1d72022c'}, {'abstract': 'A student photojournalist started out documenting the lives of a couple who gave birth to quadruplets. She now plans to stay with the story until they turn 18.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/08/what-does-life-with-quadruplets-look-like/', 'snippet': 'A student photojournalist started out documenting the lives of a couple who gave birth to quadruplets. She now plans to stay with the story until they turn 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Courtney Larson really wanted to have children. But after marrying her college sweetheart, Cameron Larson, in 2009, she learned she had fertility issues. The Larsons, who are Mormon, prayed, but, unable to get pregnant after a year, they turned to medical treatments, including intrauterine insemination. After several attempts — and thousands of dollars — she became pregnant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does Life With Quadruplets Look Like?', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Births', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molloy, Jackie (Photographer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T09:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80514863-4b12-5f2b-b37