e': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T18:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d607105-82b0-5118-a20e-60f57e075c16', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d607105-82b0-5118-a20e-60f57e075c16'}, {'abstract': 'In using the phrase “locker room talk” in a headline, The Times diminished the offensive language and actions of the Harvard men’s soccer team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/09/public-editor/why-locker-room-talk-is-no-excuse.html', 'snippet': 'In using the phrase “locker room talk” in a headline, The Times diminished the offensive language and actions of the Harvard men’s soccer team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have never been in a men’s locker room, but the news in recent weeks has offered a lesson in what to expect. First it was Donald Trump, who passed off the debasing remarks he was caught on tape making about women as mere “locker room talk.” Now it’s the Harvard men’s soccer team that was found to have crudely sexualized members of the women’s team, systematically and continually over many years. Once again, there are some who pass this behavior off as the stuff of “locker rooms.” Like who, you might ask? The New York Times, for one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/sports/11LOCKERROOMWEB04/11LOCKERROOMWEB01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why ‘Locker Room Talk’ is No Excuse', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard Crimson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T18:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None,