ith Thai and Western food. His latest venture, for which he is the creative director, is in Hell’s Kitchen, turning out Chinese dishes, a cuisine that’s not new to him since he’s part Chinese and has worked at 66, Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s Chinese restaurant in TriBeCa. “It’s never been a better time to open a Chinese restaurant now with the awareness of ingredients,” he said. And he’s having some fun making his own versions of the old standards: chicken skin dumplings, moo shu pulled beef, crispy mapo tofu, Singapore chile crab cakes and General Tso fried chicken. Desserts like flourless chocolate cake with green tea are not the usual banal afterthoughts. The room has atmosphere to spare, with lacy dark wood trellis work and Portuguese tile on the walls and underfoot. (Opens Thursday): 698 Ninth Avenue (48th Street), 212-235-1886, chaantengnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/09/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/dining/09OFF/09OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/09/dining/09OFF/09OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima