k': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/briefing/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/briefing/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/08/briefing/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/briefing/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K/09briefing-asia-slide-IZ4K-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton, Donald Trump, Mosul: Your Wednesday Briefing', 'kicker': 'Asia Pacific Edition', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T20:46:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McDermid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ddc262-c8eb-54b3-b097-0f85faaaa3e7', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ddc262-c8eb-54b3-b097-0f85faaaa3e7'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of Blackcreek Mercantile & Trading Co. created a space for his own designs alongside equally elemental works by artist friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/blackcreek-mercantile-trading-co-joshua-vogel-store.html', 'snippet': 'The founder of Blackcreek Mercantile & Trading Co. created a space for his own designs alongside equally elemental works by artist friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most people, wood is an unsexy material — the workaday stuff of foundations and flooring and furniture — but for the sculptor and designer Joshua Vogel, it is one of the most dynamic and vital substances on earth. For more than a decade, Vogel has been making deceptively simple wooden objects — tiny salt spoons, elegant sawhorse tables — according to the most rigorous principles of craftsmanship. Under the name Blackcreek Mercantile and Trading Co., which is perhaps best known for a range of understated black cutting boards, he and a small team craft by hand one-of-a-kind pieces that honor the unique qualities of the wood they carve, from the curve of a branch to artful cracks. “When I founded my studio,” Vogel explained on a recent Saturday, “I felt like I needed to break everything back down to one part, one piece, and then start over again. I wanted to focus on these very basic, pure aspects of woodworking and also the wood itself.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/t-magazine/design/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO/08tmag-black-creek-slide-KZKO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Shop for Simple, Handmade Housewares', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Store; Simple, Handmade Housewares', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kingston (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-08T21:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mimi Vu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mimi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',