ttps://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/09/business/media/media-trump-clinton.html', 'snippet': 'For not the first time this year, those analyzing this election missed what was happening all around them — and it was the story of a lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All the dazzling technology, the big data and the sophisticated modeling that American newsrooms bring to the fundamentally human endeavor of presidential politics could not save American journalism from yet again being behind the story, behind the rest of the country.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Dewey Defeats Truman’ Lesson for the Digital Age', 'kicker': 'Mediator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News Media Again Misreads Complex Pulse of the Nation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutenberg, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-09T07:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0c76af-2241-555a-b53d-62d6d709e6a4', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0c76af-2241-555a-b53d-62d6d709e6a4'}, {'abstract': 'Although Missouri has been a reliably red state in recent years, Mr. Blunt’s support of Donald J. Trump turned off some of the moderate voters who had traditionally backed him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/09/us/politics/missouri-senate-analysis.html', 'snippet': 'Although Missouri has been a reliably red state in recent years, Mr. Blunt’s support of Donald J. Trump turned off some of the moderate voters who had traditionally backed him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPRINGFIELD, Mo. — Senator Roy Blunt, Republican of Missouri, staved off an unexpectedly strong challenge on Tuesday from Jason Kander, Missouri’s secretary of state, to hold a seat Republicans had counted on to help maintain their Senate majority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt-1478637326997-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt-1478637326997-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/us/09senate-blunt2/09senate-blunt-1478637326997-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'