raph': 'In the 17th century B.C., Santorini was a small volcanic island in the Aegean Sea, home to Akrotiri, a Late Bronze Age outpost of Minoan civilization, which preceded ancient Greece. Then the volcano erupted, burying Akrotiri in ash and obliterating much of Santorini, turning it into a few smaller islands.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 506}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1727, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15OBSTSUNAMI1/15OBSTSUNAMI1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ancient Tsunami That Ended a Civilization Gets Another Look', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Ashes: A Bronze Age Chain Reaction Set in Motion by a Surge of Lava', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santorini (Greece)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek Civilization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tidal Waves and Tsunamis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crete (Greece)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nomikou, Paraskevi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-09T16:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ac23793-3094-576a-a36a-620403a4817e', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ac23793-3094-576a-a36a-620403a4817e'}, {'abstract': 'If Windows 10 annoys you and you don’t want to switch to a Mac, consider Linux or even a Chromebook instead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/technology/personaltech/finding-a-non-mac-alternative-to-microsoft.html', 'snippet': 'If Windows 10 annoys you and you don’t want to switch to a Mac, consider Linux or even a Chromebook instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I’ve always used a Windows desktop for all my business needs. My heart is with Microsoft Office, and I need to upgrade my computer, but I really dislike Windows 10. Aside from buying a Mac with Microsoft Office, can you suggest any alternatives that won’t break the bank?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Non-Mac Alternative to Microsoft', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chrome (Operating System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Linux (Operating System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-09T16:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/29163800-9b0d-5248-9fde-12613bb598aa', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29163800-9b0d-5248-9fde-12613bb598aa'}, {'abstract': 'Things happening in the world that don’t include Hillary Clinton or Donald Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/us/politics/a-quick-roundup-of-non-election-2016-news.html', 'snippet': 'Things happening in the world that don’t include Hillary Clinton or Donald Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While you were refreshing your electoral-vote map every few seconds, looking up countries to move to or running out to buy more Champagne, events unrelated to the American elections were happening in the world. Here are a few of them:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/world/10xp-other/10xp-other-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/10/world/10xp-ot