-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a0db46a-9fcc-5c30-8a14-921d5e29e926', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a0db46a-9fcc-5c30-8a14-921d5e29e926'}, {'abstract': 'As Times editors reflect on how they (and so many others) called the election so wrong, they should look at how well they cover ordinary Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/public-editor/want-to-know-what-americas-thinking-try-asking.html', 'snippet': 'As Times editors reflect on how they (and so many others) called the election so wrong, they should look at how well they cover ordinary Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the night that wasn’t supposed to happen, that had almost no chance of happening. Having relied on major media, and the overflow of polls it fed readers on a near-daily basis, the audience sat back and waited for a Democratic victory, possibly a rout. Could the Senate be reclaimed by Democrats, or even the House?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08campaign2/08campaign2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08campaign2/08campaign2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08campaign2/08campaign2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08campaign2/08campaign2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/08/us/08campaign2/08campaign2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumb