orial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/08981253-5f3d-524b-9858-8e106009ad90', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08981253-5f3d-524b-9858-8e106009ad90'}, {'abstract': 'Stunned by their good electoral fortunes, Republicans said they were eager to repeal the Affordable Care Act, cut taxes and confirm conservative judges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/us/politics/republicans-congress-paul-ryan.html', 'snippet': 'Stunned by their good electoral fortunes, Republicans said they were eager to repeal the Affordable Care Act, cut taxes and confirm conservative judges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Congressional Republicans, stunned by their own good, if complicated, fortune, said on Wednesday that they would move quickly next year on an agenda that merges with President-elect Donald J. Trump’s, repealing the Affordable Care Act, cutting taxes, confirming conservative judges, shrinking government programs and rolling back regulations.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans in Congress Plan Swift Action on Agenda With Donald Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans in Congress Plan Swift Action on Ambitious Agenda With Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11