ent made his name in real estate in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Yorkers Baffled and Anxious After Trump, One of Their Own, Clinches Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among New Yorkers, Dread and Confusion Outweigh Hometown Pride', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T02:38:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d1c14ea-33de-5234-bc80-c793d6ddd600', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d1c14ea-33de-5234-bc80-c793d6ddd600'}, {'abstract': 'Latinos fear the president-elect will pursue his mass deportation pledge, blacks anticipate an era of intolerance, and Muslims worry about being branded terrorists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/us/donald-trump-blacks-hispanics-muslims.html', 'snippet': 'Latinos fear the president-elect will pursue his mass deportation pledge, blacks anticipate an era of intolerance, and Muslims worry about being branded terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the long and contentious presidential campaign, they saw themselves on the front lines of the country’s power struggle — insulted and antagonized by Donald J. Trump and courted