line': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b0b0a4f-7280-5224-bff1-ca914f10a831', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b0b0a4f-7280-5224-bff1-ca914f10a831'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, November 10, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, November 10, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The peaceful transfer of power is one of the hallmarks of our democracy. And over the next few months, we are going to show that to the world.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T03:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/0011953d-a742-579c-9ec6-34cd7c4b1e1a', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0011953d-a742-579c-9ec6-34cd7c4b1e1a'}, {'abstract': 'Behind at halftime to the struggling Nets, the Knicks employed an offensive surge by Carmelo Anthony and a new defensive mind-set to win at the Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/sports/basketball/new-york-knicks-brooklyn-nets.html', 'snippet': 'Behind at halftime to the struggling Nets, the Knicks employed an offensive surge by Carmelo Anthony and a new defensive mind-set to win at the Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Knicks retreated into the confines of their locker room at Madison Square Garden on Wednesday night facing another ignominy. They trailed the Brooklyn Nets by 5 points at halftime and were on their way to a defeat that would only compound their early season tumult. Their defense, newly restructured and with a newly named maestro, remained shaky. Worst of all, they were trailing their crosstown rival — an organization that is using this season to rebuild and is stocked with little-known players.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/sports/10KNICKS/10KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Embarrassed’ Knicks Roll Past the Nets in the Second Half', 'kicker': 'Knicks 110, Nets 96', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Embarrassed’ Knicks Roll Past the Nets in the Second Half', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T03:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Vorkunov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vorkunov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e6317de-faa0-5268-b348-98acda0a4cdd', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e6317de-faa0-5268-b348-98acda0a4cdd'}, {'abstract': 'President Kirkman has tried in many ways to win our confidence. He’s failed in just as many.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/09/arts/television/designated-survivor-season-1-episode-6-recap.html', 'snippet': 'President Kirkman has tried in many ways to win our confidence. He’s failed in just as many.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Designated Survivor” keeps its political leanings close to the vest, perhaps in order not to alienate any one piece of its prime time network audience. But if the show stands on one fundamental principle, it’s that being the president is really, really hard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/09/watching/09designatedsurvivor2/09designatedsurvivor2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/09/watching/09designatedsurv