 on both the Democratic and Republican candidates. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Nov. 10, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/blogs/10oldiht-1916-rankin/10oldiht-1916-rankin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 489, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/blogs/10oldiht-1916-rankin/10oldiht-1916-rankin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 489, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/blogs/10oldiht-1916-rankin/10oldiht-1916-rankin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/10/blogs/10oldiht-1916-rankin/10oldiht-1916-rankin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/blogs/10oldiht-1916-rankin/10oldiht-1916-rankin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Montana Elects a Woman to Congress', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UNITED STATES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T15:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cea0a14b-27e2-5a1a-b5aa-7c116edb3976', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cea0a14b-27e2-5a1a-b5aa-7c116edb3976'}, {'abstract': 'Two gold-sculpted medallions rotate in ebony surrounded by precious stones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/t-magazine/fashion/elie-top-desdemone-necklace.html', 'snippet': 'Two gold-sculpted medallions rotate in ebony surrounded by precious stones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great jewels are made to be noticed, but in the hands of the young French designer Elie Top, the art becomes one of concealment. The elegant and mustachioed Top, who had for years designed Lanvin’s fashionable baubles, engineers much of his own namesake haute joaillerie with a mechanical precision that allows the wearer to change personalities as vividly as a peacock. Two round medallions that stud this one-of-a-kind Makassar ebony pendant are sculptured from gold. With the opening of a clasp, they rotate into the wood to reveal an intricate underside set with diamonds and colored stones like malachite, lapis, topaz and amethyst. Part of a collection called Desdémone, after the wife of Shakespeare’s passionate Moor, this substantial necklace evokes a warrior’s shield or delicate medieval stained glass.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12qual_thing_necklace-t_CA0/13tmag-12qual_thing_necklace-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12qual_thing_necklace-t_CA0/13tma