ning, desperate to exchange now-useless currency notes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crowds Line Up at India’s Banks to Exchange Banned Rupee Notes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudden Ban of Some Currency Agitates and Discomfits India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Rupee (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raj, Suhasini', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T17:41:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry and Suhasini Raj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Suhasini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1110062f-3104-5c58-8396-f3d5f3cf3460', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1110062f-3104-5c58-8396-f3d5f3cf3460'}, {'abstract': 'More than most, the tech industry was unready for the election of Donald J. Trump. Now it faces the prospect of feeling like a wary outsider. Is it?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/technology/daily-report-the-valley-awakens-to-trump.html', 'snippet': 'More than most, the tech industry was unready for the election of Donald J. Trump. Now it faces the prospect of feeling like a wary outsider. Is it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Silicon Valley loves disruption — just not, it turns out, disruptions of a certain kind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: The Valley Awakens to Trump', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T17:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa1b037d-f392-506b-b570-ee261fb3bad7', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa1b037d-f392-506b-b570-ee261fb3bad7'}, {'abstract': 'Most modern smartphones allow you to assign individual alert noises to each contact who calls or sends you a text message.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/technology/personaltech/recognize-callers-and-texters-by-sound.html', 'snippet': 'Most modern smartphones allow you to assign individual alert noises to each contact who calls or sends you a text message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. On an iPhone, is there a way to assign specific text alert sounds to different people so that you can tell who is texting without looking at the screen? The Sound settings let you assign only one text tone and one ringtone for everyone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recognize Callers and Texters by Sound', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T17:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ddb242-bfe4-5dc4-b5d3-9c21412d6021', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ddb242-bfe4-5dc4-b5d3-9c21412d6021'}, {'abstract': 'The social network for professionals was found to have violated a law requiring it to store local users’ data within the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/technology/russia-linkedin-data-court-blocked.html', 'snippet': 'The social network for professionals was found to have violated a law requiring it to store local users’ data within the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LinkedIn, the social networking site for professionals that will soon be bought by Microsoft, is to be blocked in Russia after a local court ruled on Thursday that it had breached the country’s data protection rules, a sign of growing tensions for American tech companies operating in the country.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/business/11LINKEDIN/11LINKEDIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, '