on was not a surprise. Each firm brings complementary expertise, and revenue has suffered in the changing legal landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/business/dealbook/law-firm-arnold-porter-to-merge-with-rival-kaye-scholer.html', 'snippet': 'The combination was not a surprise. Each firm brings complementary expertise, and revenue has suffered in the changing legal landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two prominent law firms, Arnold & Porter and Kaye Scholer, winding up months of talks, announced on Thursday that they would combine to become a firm with more than 1,000 lawyers effective Jan. 1. The new firm will be called Arnold & Porter Kaye Scholer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Firm Arnold & Porter to Merge With Rival Kaye Scholer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'East Coast Law Firms in a Deal to Merge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARNOLD & PORTER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaye Scholer LLP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T19:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec5d53ab-5ed4-52a8-a4dd-3223de433242', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec5d53ab-5ed4-52a8-a4dd-3223de433242'}, {'abstract': 'Canada Goose, spotted on runways of late, is opening a flagship in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/10/t-magazine/fashion/canada-goose-new-york-store.html', 'snippet': 'Canada Goose, spotted on runways of late, is opening a flagship in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lately Canada Goose, the 59-year-old outerwear brand best known for its fur-trimmed black parkas, has been found not just in wintry climes but on runways. In February, Marc Jacobs paired one of his floor-grazing sequined skirts with a men’s Manitoba coat, adding feathers, while Vetements deconstructed and puffed up two classic styles. Opening Ceremony’s (slimmer) takes were eye-catching for their use of color and print — think purple paisley. This month, Canada Goose becomes a full-fledged member of the downtown scene with the inauguration of a SoHo flagship. (It opens on the heels of a Toronto outpost, the company’s first stand-alone store.) Amid raw marble detailing sourced from British Columbia, shoppers can rest on soft maple benches by the Ontario millworker DB Johnson and other seating from the Montreal-based Montauk Sofa company. They’ll also find a celebration of soapstone-carved polar bear sculptures by the contemporary Aboriginal artist Jason Carter. “Storytelling was a crucial part of the design,” says chief executive officer Dani Reiss. “Stories like how we were there when Laurie Skreslet was the first Canadian to summit Mt. Everest.” Add to that tales of the brand’s fashion-world ascent.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/t-magazine/canada-goose/canada-goose-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/10/t-magazine/canada-goose/canada-goose-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ran