f materials as diverse as Carrara marble or plywood, maybe embedded with a moose antler. Owens’s own bed — one of an edition of three — is a monumental tomblike structure of alabaster slabs which, when combined with its matching daybed, weighs two tons.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Owens’s Monumental — if Not Entirely Cozy — Furniture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View; Anti-Cozy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fury, Alexander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T20:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Fury', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fury', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e92458a-2783-594d-bd94-fa431016502b', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e92458a-2783-594d-bd94-fa431016502b'}, {'abstract': 'The neighborhood blends old and new, with millennials living next door to decades-long residents. The shopping scene reflects a little of both, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/style/low-key-greenpoint-has-a-little-of-everything.html', 'snippet': 'The neighborhood blends old and new, with millennials living next door to decades-long residents. The shopping scene reflects a little of both, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adaptations (109 Franklin Street) is a vintage furniture store that focuses mostly on pieces from the 1970s: boxy wooden cabinets, platform sofas, macramé wall hangings and eight-track-friendly stereo receivers. Arranged like a home, with a bedroom nook in back, the store has an unintimidating atmosphere and prices that are not astronomical for items that are in excellent condition. To pair with the vintage finds there are new, plush upholstered ottomans, which the shop makes to order in a variety of fabrics.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/11/style/11GREENPOINTWEB2/11GREENPOINTWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'