rnaments and other objects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/arts/design/a-wriggle-in-time-historical-artifacts-of-belly-dancing.html', 'snippet': 'A New York teacher is keeping alive his mother’s collection of costumes, ornaments and other objects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The belly dancer Serena Wilson was so fascinated with the dance form that she wrote books about it with her husband, Alan. In their 1994 study, “The Legacy of Little Egypt: A History of the Belly Dance in America,” they described how Middle Eastern and North African performers drew crowds at Chicago and New York theaters in the 1890s and early 1900s, and how entrepreneurial Americans started learning the moves.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11ANTIQUES1/11ANTIQUES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wriggle in Time: Historical Artifacts of Belly Dancing', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wriggle in Time: Historical Artifacts of Belly Dancing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Serena (1933-2007)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T20:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c28d93d2-4340-5be9-9afc-5cb2c3df6ae0', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c28d93d2-4340-5be9-9afc-5cb2c3df6ae0'}, {'abstract': 'Soccer prospects near the United States-Mexico border face an early decision about their careers that comes with long-term consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/united-states-mexico-players.html', 'snippet': 'Soccer prospects near the United States-Mexico border face an early decision about their careers that comes with long-term consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL PASO — Night fell, and the thick, heavy air was cut by a sharp, chilling breeze, the sort of West Texas wind that made it feel as if the whole city had a fever. Was it hot out, or cold? The children on the field at Pico Norte Park — little more than a bumpy, narrow strip of grass lined for soccer — wore uniforms and quickly broke a sweat; the parents ringing the sideline wore jeans and long sleeves as they watched and cheered and occasionally shivered.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/sports/soccer/11soccer1/11soccer1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘It Is America. But I Want to Play in Mexico.’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Split Decision Along the Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guadalajara (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T20:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d9a3974-3997-54dc-a0e3-d1ee0b30989f', 'word_count': 2823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d9a3974-3997-54dc-a0e3-d1ee0b30989f'}, {'abstract': 'Also, my brother’s wife won’t come to my wedding, saying she’s afraid to fly. I don’t accept that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/13/fashion/social-qs-presidential-election-friendship-trump-supporters.html', 'snippet': 'Also, my brother’s wife won’t come to my wedding, saying she’s afraid to fly. I don’t accept that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My problem? You and idiots like you, full of straight white male privilege, who never understood the life-or-death stakes of sexism, racism and homophobia in our recent election. I heard you on the radio last week, sounding like a fool, telling people who had fought over the presidential election (and cut ties with family and friends) to look for the best in each other and talk it out. Why is it always on the victims to explain ourselves to straight men and white people? I’ve had it! After this election, I want nothing to do with any jerk who voted for Trump or limousine liberals like you. Why should I?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headli