3, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66458d76-1ab5-5d1e-b35e-57bb6832752c'}, {'abstract': 'Combatants for Peace, a group of individuals including many former military enemies in the Middle East, seeks solutions to the region’s agonized convulsions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/movies/disturbing-the-peace-review.html', 'snippet': 'Combatants for Peace, a group of individuals including many former military enemies in the Middle East, seeks solutions to the region’s agonized convulsions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How much bloodshed can a divided populace stand? In Stephen Apkon and Andrew Young’s documentary, “Disturbing the Peace,” we meet Combatants for Peace, an advocacy-activist group comprising Israelis and Palestinians who have reached their limit and renounced violence. Most are former military or paramilitary personnel seeking a two-state solution to Israel’s agonized convulsions. Their stories are compelling — and persuasive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Disturbing the Peace’ Profiles Israelis and Palestinians United Against Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review: ‘Disturbing the Peace’ Profiles Israelis and Palestinians United Against Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Combatants for Peace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Apkon, Stephen (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Andrew (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-10T21:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae81b98-85cf-55ff-9987-ecf1e443760b', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ae81b98-85cf-55ff-9987-ecf1e443760b'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Paul of “Breaking Bad” and Annabelle Wallis star as a couple torn asunder in this thriller, which Zack Whedon wrote and directed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/11/movies/come-and-find-me-review-aaron-paul.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Paul of “Breaking Bad” and Annabelle Wallis star as a couple torn asunder in this thriller, which Zack Whedon wrote and directed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his tenure on the television series “Breaking Bad,”  the actor Aaron Paul, as the foil to Bryan Cranston’s Walter White, showed an adroit skill at portraying the haplessness that can lie just below the surface of a brash game face. Mr. Paul’s role in the thriller “Come and Find Me,” as a man befuddled by the unexplained disappearance of his girlfriend (Annabelle Wallis), does not expand his performing parameters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11COMEFIND/11COMEFIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11COMEFIND/11COMEFIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/11/arts/11COMEFIND/11COMEFIND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio