nizations', 'value': 'Four Seasons Hotel George V (Paris, France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taillevent', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starck, Philippe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-11T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a26f36ff-0d2f-5a77-9cbc-0366c3610f38', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a26f36ff-0d2f-5a77-9cbc-0366c3610f38'}, {'abstract': 'Exploring (and saving money in) Washington’s Hoh Rain Forest, and the small, quirky coastal town of Port Townsend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/13/travel/washington-hoh-rainforest-port-townsend-budget-travel.html', 'snippet': 'Exploring (and saving money in) Washington’s Hoh Rain Forest, and the small, quirky coastal town of Port Townsend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was motoring along Route 101 in northwest Washington State in my little rental car, getting a kick out of the fact that I frequently drive the same highway in Southern California, where I live. There were few other similarities, though: The air in Washington had a refreshing bite to it, cold and clean. The sweet smell of wet earth seemed to follow me wherever I went, indoors or out. And soon after I left Port Angeles — a small town on the 101 that’s a quick 90-minute ferry ride to Victoria, British Columbia, across the Strait of Juan de Fuca — and entered Olympic National Park, it began to rain and didn’t stop until I left the park seven hours later.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '