, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/24/fashion/13LOVE/13LOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/fashion/13LOVE/13LOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grappling With the Language of Love', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Language Does Love Speak?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARABIC LANGUAGE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-11T15:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db801c2-ef08-5ae4-ad6e-d4d170477d61', 'word_count': 1481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db801c2-ef08-5ae4-ad6e-d4d170477d61'}, {'abstract': 'In all five boroughs, the little creature is often easier to identify with your ears than with your eyes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/13/nyregion/a-chirp-from-under-the-logs-the-fall-field-cricket.html', 'snippet': 'In all five boroughs, the little creature is often easier to identify with your ears than with your eyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As common as they are, field crickets often defy identification. Even experts resort to the plebeian measures any hiker might employ to recognize one; the plain fact is, crickets are often easier to identify with your ears than your eyes. So listening to a merry band of chirpsters singing from under a log in an empty field is often a simpler way to determine who’s calling than catching one, killing it and tacking it to a board for examination.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/13/nyregion/13NATURE/13NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumb