'}, {'abstract': 'Leading the Berlin Philharmonic in pieces by Schoenberg, Webern and Berg, Simon Rattle invited the audience to imagine that the whole was a Mahler creation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/12/arts/music/dreaming-up-a-mahler-symphony-that-never-was.html', 'snippet': 'Leading the Berlin Philharmonic in pieces by Schoenberg, Webern and Berg, Simon Rattle invited the audience to imagine that the whole was a Mahler creation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mahler’s 11th Symphony? There is no such thing. Mahler didn’t really finish his 10th Symphony, which, aside from its great opening Adagio, was left in various states of sketchiness when he died in 1911.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/12/arts/12BERLINPHIL1/12BERLINPHIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwi