t': 1387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26d8f23-4489-51e2-a3b7-c7c91d836c9b'}, {'abstract': 'Simon Morrison’s new book serves as a backstage pass to the past and present of the renowned ballet company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/14/books/review-bolshoi-confidential-peers-down-the-centuries-and-past-the-pirouettes.html', 'snippet': 'Simon Morrison’s new book serves as a backstage pass to the past and present of the renowned ballet company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Morrison’s “Bolshoi Confidential: Secrets of the Russian Ballet From the Rule of the Tsars to Today” delivers what its title promises: struggles and intrigues, crimes and punishments, imperial jewels and Soviet medals. Based on extensive research in libraries and archives, and conversations heard at Russian kitchen tables, Mr. Morrison’s book gives a historical tour behind the scenes of one of the world’s most glorious ballet institutions, from 1776, when the Bolshoi was founded by Michael Maddox, an English adventurer in Russia, to the attack with acid on Sergei Filin, the Bolshoi’s artistic director, in 2013.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/14/arts/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/14/arts/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/14/arts/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/14/arts/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB/14BOOKMORRISON3-SUB-