Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288874ba-98e9-5c0b-93b3-5ead968e03da', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288874ba-98e9-5c0b-93b3-5ead968e03da'}, {'abstract': 'A review of the election includes a look at Hillary Clinton’s struggles with blue-collar whites and why you can’t always trust exit polls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/15/upshot/how-did-trump-win-over-so-many-obama-voters.html', 'snippet': 'A review of the election includes a look at Hillary Clinton’s struggles with blue-collar whites and why you can’t always trust exit polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nate Cohn, The Upshot’s elections analyst, and Toni Monkovic, an Upshot editor, looked back at the election and posted a lightly edited transcript of their written exchange.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Did Donald Trump Win Over So Many Obama Voters?', 'kicker': 'The 2016 Race', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-14T14:01:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The U