e': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Goncharova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goncharova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1c364d-cc51-5fb5-a863-ab2cf5ce3a2f', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1c364d-cc51-5fb5-a863-ab2cf5ce3a2f'}, {'abstract': 'Six performances, including a festive 1970 jam session, recall several aspects of the musician’s career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/15/arts/music/leon-russell-playlist.html', 'snippet': 'Six performances, including a festive 1970 jam session, recall several aspects of the musician’s career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s some remarkable footage of Leon Russell from late 1970, the year he released his self-titled debut solo album. Taken from an hourlong special, “Homewood,” originally broadcast on Los Angeles public television, it circulated in bootleg editions for decades before the audio surfaced on CD this year in what appears to be a sanctioned release.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/arts/15LEONLIST/15LEONLIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/15/arts/15LEONLIST/15LEONLIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/arts/15LEONLIST/15LEONLIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/arts/15LEONLIST/15LEONLIST-superJumbo.jpg