7-1188b7189dfa'}, {'abstract': 'The $8 billion price looks fair for a company that will jump-start Samsung’s presence in the connected-car supplier market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/15/business/dealbook/samsung-takes-sensible-course-in-bid-for-harman-international.html', 'snippet': 'The $8 billion price looks fair for a company that will jump-start Samsung’s presence in the connected-car supplier market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samsung is riding a stallion instead of a unicorn into the driverless revolution. Despite no stated cost savings, the 28 percent premium the Korean electronics group agreed to pay for Harman International, a connected-car supplier, is reasonable. Companies like Google are investing heavily to invent the automotive future as General Motors and others bet on risky start-ups. This deal suggests there are safer ways to play a mega-trend in the making.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samsung Takes Sensible Course in Bid for Harman International', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alphabet Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-14T20:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'ny