': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc3456c1-1d21-5703-893b-4f975fe827b8', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc3456c1-1d21-5703-893b-4f975fe827b8'}, {'abstract': 'For decades, young reporters and news assistants at The Times have begun their careers on the Neediest Cases beat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/nyregion/neediest-cases-reporters-lesson.html', 'snippet': 'For decades, young reporters and news assistants at The Times have begun their careers on the Neediest Cases beat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly a quarter-century ago, as a junior reporter in our newsroom, I received one of the most significant assignments of my career: writing stories about the many people helped by The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 847}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy/16INSIDER-NEEDIEST-levy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reporter’s Lesson: Giving a Voice to the Ignored', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Reporter’s Lesson: Giving a Voice to People Often Ignored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-15T16:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford J. Levy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Levy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48eafdca-1bea-5a0d-8e69-594e2164df75', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48eafdca-1bea-5a0d-8e69-594e2164df75'}, {'abstract': 'Gregory Manson, 43, knows the importance of having a roof over his head after bouncing around shelters and transitional living facilities in the Bronx, Manhattan and Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/nyregion/after-a-lifetime-of-instability-hoping-for-a-place-to-touch-down.html', 'snippet': 'Gregory Manson, 43, knows the importance of having a roof over his head after bouncing around shelters and transitional living facilities in the Bronx, Manhattan and Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gregory Manson has moved so many times that he struggles to remember all of the dates, the neighborhoods and the family members he has stayed with. There was his stepmother in Canarsie, Brooklyn, a sister in Jamaica, Queens, and his grandmother’s apartment in the Farragut Houses in Brooklyn. It is all blended and blurred.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/nyregion/16neediestmanson/16neediestmanson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Lifetime of Instability, Hoping for a Place to Touch Down', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoping for a Home After a Lifetime of Instability', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Community Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-15T16:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terence McGinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b59ea65-2066-5716-bfad-8697971a848d', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b59ea65-2066-5716-bfad-8697971a848d'}, {'abstract': 'A new state grant program is aimed at creating urban settings to support entrepreneurs and attract younger workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/realestate/commercial/hartford-kicks-open-its-doors-to-innovators.html', 'snippet': 'A new state grant program is aimed at creating urban settings to support entrepreneurs and attract younger workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — After Lelaneia Dubay developed an intolerance for the gluten and chemical additives in many alcoholic beverages, she went looking for a way to salvage her cocktail hour. Already skilled at making cranberry liqueur, which she bottled and gave as