iddlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Radomsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8330e2a3-55ca-5e0c-a823-0d867145d233', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8330e2a3-55ca-5e0c-a823-0d867145d233'}, {'abstract': 'One of the essential 1990s hip-hop groups is back with its first album in 18 years, an often stunning work that interweaves social and political truth-telling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/arts/music/a-tribe-called-quest.html', 'snippet': 'One of the essential 1990s hip-hop groups is back with its first album in 18 years, an often stunning work that interweaves social and political truth-telling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the music business, when you disappear for a long stretch of time, you abandon your right to grouse about how things have changed in your absence. Nostalgia is a cheap crutch and a lame weapon. When the whole world is changing, though, disappearing and then re-emerging in different circumstances can be more deeply destabilizing. The things you held dear might be missing, or under attack. Adjusting is a full-time job.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/arts/16TRIBEQUESTJP/16TRIBEQUESTJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/16/arts/16TRIBEQUESTJP/16TRIBEQUESTJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/arts/16TRIBEQUESTJP/16TRIBEQUESTJP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred