: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb3b7354-5fb5-5ae4-abbd-e7a70b58912b', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb3b7354-5fb5-5ae4-abbd-e7a70b58912b'}, {'abstract': 'In “Thank You for Coming: Play,” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, her dancers are delving into the social experience of storytelling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/arts/dance/exploring-the-space-between-performer-and-audience.html', 'snippet': 'In “Thank You for Coming: Play,” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, her dancers are delving into the social experience of storytelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a studio at the Brooklyn Academy of Music on a recent afternoon, a few dancers stood around chatting, as if catching up before rehearsal. Yet the conversation, upon closer listening, sounded warped, like a script chopped up and scrambled. Gestures, words and facial expressions didn’t quite match up, tricking the mind into seeking a clear, coherent message that never arrived.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/17/arts/17DRISCOLL/16DRISCOLL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/17/arts/17DRISCOLL/16DRISCOLL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/17/arts/17DRISCOLL/16DRISCOLL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/17/arts/17DRISCOLL/16DRISCOLL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/17/arts/17DRISCOLL/16DRISCOLL1-articl