m/2016/11/16/nyregion/cuny-investigation-report-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'The New York State inspector general cited financial mismanagement and poor oversight in its first formal review of the university system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shoddy oversight and ineffective management at the City University of New York have created a system “ripe for abuse” that has potentially siphoned money away from needy students and crucial campus projects, according to a report released on Tuesday by the New York State inspector general.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lapses by CUNY Officials Made System ‘Ripe for Abuse,’ Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poor Oversight Made CUNY Finances ‘Ripe for Abuse,’ State Inspector General Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, David W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City College of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn College, City University of New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milliken, James B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staiano-Coico, Lisa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T01:36:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0b11b19-0243-59b2-8443-e15d0d459a43', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0b11b19-0243-59b2-8443-e15d0d459a43'}, {'abstract': 'While discussing her new book, the Fox News anchor describes her initial run-in with Donald J. Trump as “prescient” and warns fellow journalists to remain vigilant while covering the Trump White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/business/media/megyn-kellys-cautionary-tale-of-crossing-donald-j-trump.html', 'snippet': 'While discussing her new book, the Fox News anchor describes her initial run-in with Donald J. Trump as “prescient” and warns fellow journalists to remain vigilant while covering the Trump White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fox News anchor Megyn Kelly has spent the better part of the last year living in the main gladiator pit of 2016, becoming as much a target for Donald J. Trump as any of his opponents and emerging as a pivotal figure in the forced resignation of the Fox News Channel chairman Roger Ailes, whom she accused of sexual harassment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/business/16RUTENBERG/16RUTENBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/16/business/16RUTENBERG/16RUTENBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/business/16RUTENBERG/16RUTENBERG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 804, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/16/business/16RUTE