e': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15PHYSED/15PHYSED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/science/15PHYSED/15PHYSED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for: ‘Eye Injuries in Youth Sports Are Surprisingly Common’', 'kicker': 'Article of the Day', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T09:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53132eb1-136a-5b12-9ca7-967aa467ab61', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53132eb1-136a-5b12-9ca7-967aa467ab61'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on what a child owes an aging parent, who is entitled to read a found letter and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/magazine/am-i-obliged-to-support-my-elderly-mother.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on what a child owes an aging parent, who is entitled to read a found letter and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently graduated from college — the first person in my family to do so — and am trying to make a life for myself in New York. My father passed away several months ago, and my mother, who is in her 70s, is incapable of financial independence. She has never been financially responsible, and now the burden has fallen on my shoulders, because she has no family and I’m an only child. In my view, she lives way beyond her means; each time I suggest that she cut out a few expenses (fewer trips to the beauty parlor, shopping at a discount market), she breaks down and often lashes out at me. I fear that if I continue to support her, I’ll never be able to save enough money for my own future. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 868}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 972, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 972, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/magazine/20ethicist/20ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Am I Obliged to Support My Elderly Mother?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr