,’ on TBS, the Real Quest Is for the Self', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; The Search Is for the Self', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Search Party (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TBS Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shawkat, Alia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bliss, Sarah-Violet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Charles (1987- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Showalter, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T16:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9591275-5705-53a5-aa21-56be7ba84626', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9591275-5705-53a5-aa21-56be7ba84626'}, {'abstract': 'Professional choreographers work with students, and both sides benefit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/arts/dance/juilliards-new-dances-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'Professional choreographers work with students, and both sides benefit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When professional choreographers work with students, both sides benefit: Students are exposed to new ways of moving (and possible future employers), while artists can try out ideas on large, curious groups. The Juilliard Dance Division’s winter concert, “New Dances,” facilitates that kind of exchange, and the Guggenheim Museum presents a sneak peek of this year’s offerings — by John Heginbotham, Katarzyna Skarpetowska, Pam Tanowitz and Matthew Neenan, each working with a different class — on Sunday, Nov. 20, as part of its Works & Process series.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1277}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 482, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE2/20GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juilliard’s ‘New Dances’ at the Guggenheim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Students Moving in New Ways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard Dance Division', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heginbotham, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neenan, Matthew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skarpetowska, Katarzyna', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanowitz, Pam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T16:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8205aa3-c735-59ea-ac46-daab04ad236b', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8205aa3-c735-59ea-ac46-daab04ad236b'}, {'abstract': 'The Dewberry is a midcentury masterpiece (and a great place to enjoy a highball).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/16/t-magazine/travel/dewberry-hotel-charleston-south-carolina-workstead.html', 'snippet': 'The Dewberry is a midcentury masterpiece (and a great place to enjoy a highball).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workstead, a rising design firm, makes its South Carolina debut with the Dewberry, a 155-room hotel built in the shell of the 1964 L. Mendel Rivers Federal Building overlooking Charleston’s Marion Square. “We wanted to explore the idea of Southern Modernism,” says co-founder Robert Highsmith. Taking cues from Milan’s Villa Necchi Campiglio, Havana’s Hotel Nacional, and Slim Aarons, they mixed midcentury Danish antiques with nods to the Lowcountry, such as oak salvaged from a tobacco barn in Georgia.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '68', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/15/t-magazine/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO/dewberry-hotel-slide-NWJO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet Southern Hospitality in a New Charleston Hotel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southern Hospitality ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Workstead', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T16:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Talbot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Talbot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/537fe960-27bf-5ec2-a3cf-d480107bfd7c', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/537fe960-27bf-5ec2-a3cf-d480107bfd7c'}, {'abstract': 'The new-music ensemble Counter)Induction devotes an evening to the work of one guy named Moe: Eric Moe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/arts/music/a-feast-of-one-composers-dreamy-reticence-and-rhythmic-irascibility.html', 'snippet': 'The new-music ensemble Counter)Induction devotes an evening to the work of one guy named Moe: Eric Moe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dramatic instinct and poetic sensibility are the hallmarks of Eric Moe’s music; his compositional voice is always distinct, whether in works of dreamy reticence or rhythmic irascibility. On Sunday, Nov. 20, the trailblazing new-music ensemble Counter)Induction dedicates an evening to Mr. Moe that is also an advertisement for the kind of composer-performer symbiosis that has proved so fertile across the New York scene. Half of the program, presented at National Sawdust, is given over to works by Mr. Moe, including a conversation for acoustic viola and electronics, “What Instruments We Have Agree,” an elegy on the death of the composer Lee Hyla, and the New York premiere of “Welcome to Phase Space,” enigmatically described as representing an eight-dimensional universe.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE4/20GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2007, 'width': 2007, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Feast of One Composer’s Dreamy Reticence and Rhythmic Irascibility', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical; Dreamy Reticence, Irascible Rhythm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Sawdust (Brooklyn, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moe, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations