r/nicky-silvers-this-day-forward-kicks-off-vineyards-season.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Silver’s latest comedy is directed by Mark Brokaw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicky Silver has had a fruitful relationship with the Vineyard Theater since 1993, when his absurdist comedy “Pterodactyls” had its Off Broadway premiere there. More of his quirky works followed, including, in 2011, “The Lyons,” which starred Linda Lavin and moved to Broadway the following year. (The show marked Mr. Silver’s Broadway debut, an experience he wrote about after it closed.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 276}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20GUIDE1/20GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'