ani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-16T21:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f11290b0-0c5a-534a-a7b5-7a7341020304', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f11290b0-0c5a-534a-a7b5-7a7341020304'}, {'abstract': 'He will play the title role in a modern-dress production of “Othello,” featuring the action star Daniel Craig.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/theater/david-oyelowo-othello-new-york-theater-workshop.html', 'snippet': 'He will play the title role in a modern-dress production of “Othello,” featuring the action star Daniel Craig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a long time, the British-Nigerian actor David Oyelowo didn’t want to play Othello. Years ago, before his move from London to Los Angeles, a few producers approached him. He turned them down. He loved Shakespeare, of course, but the roles that excited him were Coriolanus, Macbeth, Henry V. Not the Moor. “I don’t want to do anything that feels pedestrian or obvious,” he said.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20OYELOWO1/20OYELOWO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20OYELOWO1/20OYELOWO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/arts/20OYELOWO1/20OYELOWO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thu