dlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2576a6b-cc97-59ae-aef9-1557f5ee11b3', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2576a6b-cc97-59ae-aef9-1557f5ee11b3'}, {'abstract': '“A.H.S.” has always been polarizing, and critics are divided on whether the episode brought “Roanoke” to a satisfying end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/17/watching/american-horror-story-roanoke-finale.html', 'snippet': '“A.H.S.” has always been polarizing, and critics are divided on whether the episode brought “Roanoke” to a satisfying end.', 'lead_paragraph': '“American Horror Story” creator Ryan Murphy wasn’t kidding when he casually mentioned, weeks before the premiere of Season 6, that the seasons in his anthology horror series are all connected. Wednesday night’s finale not only culminated the show’s meta-commentary on celebrity, violence and television, it also served as the final piece tying together all six of its seasons. “A.H.S.” has always been a polarizing series, and critics are divided on whether the high-concept episode brought “Roanoke” to a satisfying end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/17/watching/american-horror-story-watching09/american-horror-story-watching09-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/17/watching/american-horror-story-watching09/american-horror-story-watching09-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/17/watching/american-horror-story-watching09/american-horror-story-watching09-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': '