llows a man to rehab, and includes the aftermath of an alcohol-induced auto accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Belgian documentary “Ne Me Quitte Pas” (“Don’t Leave Me”) begins with a bang, so to speak. A man and a woman are discussing their marriage, or soon-to-be lack thereof; the woman is leaving him. The man, drawing from a can of beer, casually requests sex from her one last time. Befuddled, she refuses. He presses the issue, wryly, or, rather, in a tone that he believes to be wry. “You’ll forget me in no time,” the woman says with firmness and equanimity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 278, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 278}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 950, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18NEMEQUITTE/18NEMEQUITTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur