Vehicles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porsche AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6914b939-89fb-53dc-b645-c9914701927f', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6914b939-89fb-53dc-b645-c9914701927f'}, {'abstract': 'With Bob on his shoulder, a homeless busker, James, is able to face just about anything — a negligent father, street ruffians and drug withdrawal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/movies/a-street-cat-named-bob-review-luke-treadaway.html', 'snippet': 'With Bob on his shoulder, a homeless busker, James, is able to face just about anything — a negligent father, street ruffians and drug withdrawal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Grumpy Cat and “Keanu” haven’t sated your appetite for screen felines, try “A Street Cat Named Bob,” a savvy exercise in inspirational feel-good cinema lightly seasoned with grit. Adapted from James Bowen’s autobiography (part of a Bob franchise), the movie, directed by Roger Spottiswoode, tells how an orange cat enters the life of James (Luke Treadaway), a homeless London busker struggling with heroin addiction. Though James has a sobriety adviser (a firm Joanne Froggatt, as a persuasive living argument for public health care) who finds him housing, it is the cat, which James names Bob, who teaches him about responsibility and what it’s like to feel loved.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 714}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 862, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18STREETART/18STREETART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1723, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘A Street Cat Named Bob’ Helps His Owner Detox', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Treadaway, Luke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowen, James (1979- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spottiswoode, Roger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3faa5a58-f787-5abf-885e-a3518f6d26df', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3faa5a58-f787-5abf-885e-a3518f6d26df'}, {'abstract': 'Putting the two together will yield a green-energy company whose products include electric cars and solar panels for homes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/business/dealbook/tesla-and-solarcity-shareholders-approve-merger.html', 'snippet': 'Putting the two together will yield a green-energy company whose products include electric cars and solar panels for homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALM SPRINGS, Calif. — Elon Musk has succeeded in combining two parts of his business empire, as investors in Tesla Motors and in the solar panel maker SolarCity agreed on Thursday to a merger.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tesla and SolarCity Shareholders Approve Merger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shareholders  O.K. Merger of SolarCity  and Tesla', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Merced, Michael J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SolarCity Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17c4f74b-19cf-52be-9e7d-10c2a8ce2fb8', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17c4f74b-19cf-52be-9e7d-10c2a8ce2fb8'}, {'abstract': 'Brooklyn Touring Outfit’s “Co. Venture” explores the ties between the dancer Pepper Fajans, 31, and David Vaughan, 92, a former Merce Cunningham archivist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/arts/dance/review-a-cross-generational-bond-conveyed-in-dance.html', 'snippet': 'Brooklyn Touring Outfit’s “Co. Venture” explores the ties between the dancer Pepper Fajans, 31, and David Vaughan, 92, a former Merce Cunningham archivist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Vaughan first met Pepper Fajans, it was not in Mr. Fajans’s capacity as a dancer (which he is), but as a carpenter (which he also is). Mr. Fajans was building a set for “Mondays With Merce,” a video series devoted to the work of the choreographer Merce Cunningham. Mr. Vaughan was the Cunningham company’s longtime archivist; Mr. Fajans eventually became Cunningham’s caretaker for 10 months until his death in 2009 and then, during the company’s final tour, looked after Mr. Vaughan. Despite their difference in ages — Mr. Vaughan is 92, Mr. Fajans 31 — they formed a deep bond.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/TOURING/TOURING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Cross-Generational Bond, Conveyed in Dance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Man and Young, Soldered by Layers of Understanding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fajans, Pepper (1985- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaughan, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Touring Outfit', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Co Venture (Dance)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8de36264-e72a-51d0-b78b-58c389dba28e', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8de36264-e72a-51d0-b78b-58c389dba28e'}, {'abstract': 'Tips on how to navigate the holiday in an especially polarized climate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/fashion/social-qs-thanksgiving-edition.html', 'snippet': 'Tips on how to navigate the holiday in an especially polarized climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My son is my only child. When he was 4, I divorced his father and raised him on my own. I didn’t receive any financial support, so I worked full time to support us. Now my son is married with three children. But since he married, I am not included in family holidays like Thanksgiving or Christmas. For years, I invited them, but they never accepted. They spend holidays with my daughter-in-law’s family. It bothers me that my in-laws don’t seem to care that I’m left alone. I’ve had many talks with my son about this, but nothing changes. Is there anything more I can do?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dumped Moms, Gun-Toting Guests: It’s Thanksgiving', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dumped by a Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e603f348-da65-5b37-9b64-9e0c2f4e3e44', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e603f348-da65-5b37-9b64-9e0c2f4e3e44'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama, appearing with Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany, also warned Donald J. Trump to take the presidency seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/world/europe/obama-angela-merkel-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama, appearing with Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany, also warned Donald J. Trump to take the presidency seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — In his strongest public comments since the election, President Obama on Thursday sharply criticized the spread of fake news online and said that President-elect Donald J. Trump would not remain in office for long if he failed to take the job seriously.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, With Angela Merkel in Berlin, Assails Spread of Fake News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Assails Fake News and Warns Trump to Take Job Seriously', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:43:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris and Mel