ly in his career, and his nephew Aaron Brookner, now also a filmmaker.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Uncle Howard” begins with a scene portraying its director, Aaron Brookner, as a man on a mission. Filmed with a shaky video camera, he follows the poet John Giorno into his apartment, hot on the trail of a cache of films made by Mr. Brookner’s uncle, Howard Brookner.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Uncle Howard’ Looks Back at a Filmmaker’s Work Cut Short', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Back at the Arc of a Filmmaker’s Career', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Uncle Howard (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giorno, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brookner, Aaron (1981- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brookner, Howard (1954-89)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:50:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c2744b-f6ee-53c5-8d92-c96da8a01e45', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c2744b-f6ee-53c5-8d92-c96da8a01e45'}, {'abstract': '“With All Due Respect” will terminate as Bloomberg reshuffles its politics team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/business/media/bloomberg-to-end-its-daily-politics-show.html', 'snippet': '“With All Due Respect” will terminate as Bloomberg reshuffles its politics team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the election now in the rearview mirror, Bloomberg has decided to terminate its daily politics show “With All Due Respect” hosted by the political journalists John Heilemann and Mark Halperin and refocus its Bloomberg Politics team, according to a staff memo on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/business/18BLOOMBERG/18BLOOMBERG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg to End Its Daily Politics Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg to End Show on Politics in Revamping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg TV', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halperin, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heilemann, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1686143-13cb-5f0a-9f8f-16c667cdf721', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1686143-13cb-5f0a-9f8f-16c667cdf721'}, {'abstract': 'In its grandest project yet, the concert series Wordless Music will screen Terrence Malick’s film with live accompaniment at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/arts/music/wordless-music-the-tree-of-life-brooklyn-academy-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'In its grandest project yet, the concert series Wordless Music will screen Terrence Malick’s film with live accompaniment at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronen Givony, who founded the omnivorous concert series Wordless Music, is often surprised that he’s the first to pounce on a new musical opportunity. In 2008, he faced no competition from major orchestras in vying to give the American premiere of a piece by Radiohead’s Jonny Greenwood. And several years ago, he broke out of the pops-like mold of film-soundtrack karaoke with a live performance of the magical Cajun-inspired score for “Beasts of the Southern Wild.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18TREELIFE1/18TREELIFE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1216, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Tree of Life’ Unfurls, With a Live Orchestra and Choir', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Tree of Life’ Sonically Unfurls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Tree of Life (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malick, Terrence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAdams, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Givony, Ronen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wordless Music Orchestra', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T21:51:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f39c9c6f-f796-575d-843a-ee11e5e59677', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f39c9c6f-f796-575d-843a-ee11e5e59677'}, {'abstract': 'The troupe, visiting from The Hague, is presenting four works from its repertory of contemporary ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/arts/dance/review-nederlands-dans-theater-prizes-procedure-over-passion.html', 'snippet': 'The troupe, visiting from The Hague, is presenting four works from its repertory of contemporary ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most technically proficient dancers aren’t always the ones who can make us feel most deeply. Take, for example, Nederlands Dans Theater, which returned to City Center on Wednesday. It appears there’s nothing that this limpid troupe can’t do, in terms of stretching the body to spectacular extremes. Yet for the most part, the choreography the dancers so impeccably master limits them to showing off.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/1