g set of luggage in the back seat and a slightly contrasting shade of lipstick on her mouth and on the stubbed-out cigarettes in the car’s ashtray. Later on, red wine will be spilled, and there will be blood from various sources.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/arts/18LOVEWITCH/18LOVEWITCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Love Witch,’ Hell-Bent on Capturing Your Heart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dark Seductress, Hell-Bent on Capturing Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Love Witch (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Samantha (1991- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biller, Anna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-17T22:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c207e618-71f9-5a2b-901c-109473acead5', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c207e618-71f9-5a2b-901c-109473acead5'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Irving’s documentary is the story of Darius McCollum, a man with Asperger’s syndrome who borrows trains and buses for joy rides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/movies/off-the-rails-review.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Irving’s documentary is the story of Darius McCollum, a man with Asperger’s syndrome who borrows trains and buses for joy rides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The documentary “Off the Rails,” Adam Irving’s first film, is an assured and thoughtful debut. He presents the story of Darius McCollum, a man with a long history of taking New York City subway trains and buses for joy rides even though he is not a transit employee. But Mr. Irving’s subtext is a criminal justice system that has no way to deal with an offender like Mr. McCollum, who has Asperger’s syndrome, other than to keep throwing him in prison.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Off the Rails,’ an Eager Conductor Stalks New York’s Transit System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Ne