thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/19/sports/19panthers-web1/19panthers-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/19/sports/19panthers-web1/19panthers-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Carolina Panthers Survive Their 1-5 Start? Uh, No', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Panthers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-18T15:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58bcdfb3-3368-52b6-af51-fb99eac9d307', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58bcdfb3-3368-52b6-af51-fb99eac9d307'}, {'abstract': 'Our secessionary mood is an emotional reaction to the election of Donald Trump and a reflection of the power of our own brand of liberalism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/i-wish-we-all-could-be-californian.html', 'snippet': 'Our secessionary mood is an emotional reaction to the election of Donald Trump and a reflection of the power of our own brand of liberalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'San Francisco — THIS is going to sound very California, but here goes: I drowned my election sorrows by surfing. It didn’t help, but I was struck by something afterward. All my life, I’ve seen strangers on California beaches — bearded bodysurfers drinking local Bourbon, Republican volleyball players eating vegan energy bars — trade warm glances that say, “I salute your lifestyle choices and respect your privacy.” After the election, those furtive nods implied nausea, terror and a compassion born of confidence that others felt much the same. Within that compassion, I sensed the emergence of something new in California public life: an awareness that we Californians are bound together as one people by the shared values of our increasingly tolerant and pluralistic society.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/opinion/sunday/20duane/20duane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 