e', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/be27ddaf-2081-5eb9-9d92-8154f5615d84', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be27ddaf-2081-5eb9-9d92-8154f5615d84'}, {'abstract': 'In two developments on Friday, the wrestlers apologized for their lewd and racist text messages, and the university announced their punishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/19/sports/columbia-wrestlers-apologize-for-texts-in-open-letter.html', 'snippet': 'In two developments on Friday, the wrestlers apologized for their lewd and racist text messages, and the university announced their punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Columbia University said Friday that it would punish members of its wrestling team who had shared lewd and racist text messages and that the remainder of the team had been cleared to resume competition.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Columbia Disciplines Wrestlers and Clears Team to Return to Competition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Texting Scandal, Columbia Allows Some Wrestlers to Return', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Seth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wrestling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-18T16:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78067af4-eb0a-5d10-a58a-1b1c091fef4d', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78067af4-eb0a-5d10-a58a-1b1c091fef4d'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t betray America, and the world.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/18/the-sorrow-and-the-pity/', 'snippet': 'Don’t betray America, and the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of people in politics and the media are scrambling to normalize what just happened to us, saying that it will all be OK and we can work with Trump. No, it won’t, and no, we can’t. The next occupant of the White House will be a pathological liar with a loose grip on reality; he is already surrounding himself with racists, anti-Semites, and conspiracy theorists; his administration will be the most corrupt in America history. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sorrow and the Pity', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-18T16:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3291330f-2735-5d68-b01c-1d7bace1a063', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3291330f-2735-5d68-b01c-1d7bace1a063'}, {'abstract': 'During the campaign, followers drawn to his rallies occasionally displayed the flag. Since the election, his suppor