reater opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/20/books/review/race-in-america-after-the-great-migration.html', 'snippet': 'New books examine race in America in the time since millions of black migrants moved in hopes of greater opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A century ago, almost all black Americans lived in the South, largely in rural areas. By 1970, most lived outside the South, a great many in Northern and Western industrial cities. Driven, in part, by hopes for greater economic opportunity, millions of black migrants made this move. Did they find what they were looking for?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 883, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 883}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/books/review/1120-BKS-IvoryTower/1120-BKS-IvoryTower-jumbo.jpg', 'hei