r-please-stand-up.html', 'snippet': 'A nonprofit that disputes huge bills from a supplier of printer toner is whipsawed between two companies, one of which is not even supposed to exist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Haggler loves a great consumer mystery. Like, why are hotel thermostats so varied and confounding? Do we really need smart refrigerators? And here’s one that recently flitted across the Haggler’s mind: When Taco Bell conceived its Cheesy Core Burrito — basically, a cheese burrito stuffed inside a beef burrito — did it ever consider cramming the whole concoction into yet another, even bigger burrito and calling it the Triple Dare?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 578}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 986, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1926, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/business/20HAGGLER/20HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':