on': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Apple Empowers, and Employs, the American Working Class', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Apple Empowers, and Employs, the American Working Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-20T21:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vindu Goel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vindu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2d97e4-654e-50af-aa46-537d1337093b', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2d97e4-654e-50af-aa46-537d1337093b'}, {'abstract': 'If conductors can be divided into those who excel at Brahms’s First and Third symphonies and those who do best with the Second and Fourth, Andris Nelsons is the former.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/21/arts/music/review-brahms-at-the-boston-smphony-with-helene-grimaud.html', 'snippet': 'If conductors can be divided into those who excel at Brahms’s First and Third symphonies and those who do best with the Second and Fourth, Andris Nelsons is the former.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The British critic Richard Osborne once wrote that, when it comes to Brahms’s symphonies, there are First and Third conductors, and Second and Fourth conductors. The scheme is loose and doesn’t apply to everyone, particularly not to visionaries or stoics, but it captures the difficulties in maintaining consistency across the cycle. Musicians who excel in the personal, odd-numbered statements are often challenged, relatively speaking, by the formalistic, even-numbered works.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21BSO/21BSO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Brahms at the Boston Smphony, With Hélène Grimaud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Symphonic Celebration of Brahms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimaud, Helene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brahms, Johannes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelsons, Andris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andres, Timo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-20T22:05:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b1542c8-eb0e-51ea-8be1-7b93c3243ea8', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b1542c8-eb0e-51ea-8be1-7b93c3243ea8'}, {'abstract': 'A cure for millennial malaise? Maybe, at least for the sleuths who pursue this mystery, and the humor it exudes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/21/arts/television/review-search-party-alia-shawkat.html', 'snippet': 'A cure for millennial malaise? Maybe, at least for the sleuths who pursue this mystery, and the humor it exudes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a television season full of nonconformist new comedies, TBS’s “Search Party,” beginning Monday, is one of the odder ducks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21SEARCHPARTY/21SEARCHPARTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/21/arts/21SEARCH