— A couple visiting Morocco in the 1970s gave in to the temptation of the Marrakesh bazaar and bought a silver brooch, never dreaming that the purchase would lead to many more over the years in other North African souks or from dealers in Paris. Now, the collection of the Swiss couple, Jean-François and Malou Bouvier, is being shown for the first time at “Wearable Treasures: Jewelry and Accessories,” an exhibition through Jan. 8 at the Institute of the Arab World in Paris. The museum’s director, Eric Delpont, spoke recently about the exhibition curated by Djamila Chakour. This interview has been condensed and edited.', 'print_section': 'S', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/style/22MAGHREB01-INYT/22MAGHREB01-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', '