nfront budget cuts and public distrust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/21/opinion/policing-flint.html', 'snippet': 'Step inside the Police Department of Flint, Mich., to see how officers in this struggling city confront budget cuts and public distrust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As filmmakers, we’ve always been interested in exploring different mediums to combine intimate, character-driven stories with a strong sense of place. We employed this approach while making our first feature documentary, “T-Rex,” about the two-time Olympic gold medal boxer Claressa Shields, who is a native of the once thriving, now struggling, city of Flint, Mich. After spending four years in the city and getting to know its residents, we felt there was more that needed to be told about the challenges Flint is confronting. So last fall, we began production on an episodic documentary series about an institution at the core of the city, the Flint Police Department.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Policing Flint', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Reality (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flint (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-21T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zackary Canepari and Drea Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zackary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Canepari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Drea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': N