a-af67-c1cdcd5fe9e9'}, {'abstract': 'With Donald Trump headed to the White House, my future as a working community college student is uncertain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/21/opinion/a-dreamers-deportation-nightmare.html', 'snippet': 'With Donald Trump headed to the White House, my future as a working community college student is uncertain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTAGE, Ind. — I was working the night of the election — helping ship merchandise to convenience stores around Indiana — so I kept up on the news by texting a friend. “Should I worry?” I asked around 10 p.m. Not yet, he said. An hour later, the response had changed: “Pressing the worry button now.” I got off work at midnight, and listened to the radio as I drove home. It was by then Nov. 9, and the election was coming to an end. But it didn’t hit me until I saw my mom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/opinion/21oncampusWeb/21oncampusWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/21/opinion/21oncampusWeb/21oncampusWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/opinion/21oncampusWeb/21oncampusWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/opinion/21oncampusWeb/21concampusWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/21/opinion/21oncampusWeb/21concampusWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre