l': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/21/t-magazine/design/london-design-museum-kensington-high-street.html', 'snippet': 'One museum reopens with a new look — and a free exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a busy year for London’s design world. Fall marked the city’s inaugural Design Biennale, and now the Design Museum is entering an ambitious era in its new home on Kensington High Street, on the edge of Holland Park. The interior of the former Commonwealth Institute building, reimagined by John Pawson, will triple the museum’s exhibition space. Despite the soaring, vast scope of the space (crowned with a dramatic paraboloid roof), Pawson aimed to create a welcoming environment. “I used lots of warm wood and made sure there were benches and seating areas to encourage people to stay for a while.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/t-magazine/design-museum-slide-1E7A/design-museum-slide-1E7A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/21/t-magazine/design-museum-slide-1E7A/design-museum-slide-1E7A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 496}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/t-magazine/design-museum-slide-1E7A/design-museum-slide-1E7A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/21/t-magazine/design-museum-slide-1E7A/design-museum-slide-1E7A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1694, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/1