d worker — they’re rooted in a real dynamic. Many of the most skilled workers — young people with college degrees — are leaving struggling regions of America for cities, specifically for cities in Southern and coastal states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The States That College Graduates Are Most Likely to Leave', 'kicker': 'Moving On', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unwelcome Exodus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bui, Quoctrung', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-22T12:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quoctrung Bui', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quoctrung', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6945e97-77f8-5393-91ba-a3ebc252dc48', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6945e97-77f8-5393-91ba-a3ebc252dc48'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Revkin argues that a first step toward a successful human journey is a little positive self regard.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/22/rx-for-the-anthropocene-a-dose-of-anthropophilia/', 'snippet': 'Andy Revkin argues that a first step toward a successful human journey is a littl