News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd8b6e32-a122-57e2-b537-0c66c8e11eb5', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd8b6e32-a122-57e2-b537-0c66c8e11eb5'}, {'abstract': 'Have you been following the news? Take our quiz to see what you know and to learn more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/22/learning/weekly-news-quiz-nov-15-21-2016.html', 'snippet': 'Have you been following the news? Take our quiz to see what you know and to learn more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congratulations! Last week most everyone did very well on our quiz, missing only the question about global temperatures. (To recap: Climate scientists worry that 2016 is on track to be the hottest year recorded to date. If so, that would break the record set in 2015, which broke the record set in 2014.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/22/us/22legal-2-LN/22legal-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'j