 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T08:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/45085f90-997f-501a-a99d-4e233750903a', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45085f90-997f-501a-a99d-4e233750903a'}, {'abstract': 'I made the choice to sacrifice social acceptability for the freedom to be myself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/opinion/my-life-with-tourettes-syndrome.html', 'snippet': 'I made the choice to sacrifice social acceptability for the freedom to be myself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 17, my father took me to a juvenile treatment clinic to see if doctors could figure out what was wrong with me. I entered a room. I sat on a chair. I waited for a long while. There was a video camera trained on me. Then I heard voices, the voices of doctors behind a two-way mirror. It was like being in a police interrogation room in the movies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/opinion/23disability/23disability-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Life With Tourette’s Syndrome', 'kicker': 'Disability', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Life With Tourette Syndrome', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Tourette's Syndrome", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T08:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane Fistell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fistell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/455f83b9-0102-5b15-a84e-0579d615bfe6', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/455f83b9-0102-5b15-a84e-0579d615bfe6'}, {'abstract': 'Reports of domestic workers falling to their deaths this year have added urgency to a long-running debate about the city’s reliance on low-cost migrant labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/world/asia/hong-kong-migrants-domestic-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Reports of domestic workers falling to their deaths this year have added urgency to a long-running debate about the city’s reliance on low-cost migrant labor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Whenever the windows of her employer’s 35th-floor apartment looked dirty, Win Win Warsiating would lean halfway out of the high-rise building to clean them. Sometimes she would glance down at the ground far below and be seized with anxiety, she said. But she never complained.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/20/world/22HONGHELPER-1/22HONGHELPER-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Window-Washing Deaths, a Debate Over Migrants’ Rights in Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High-Rise Falls Prompt Debate Over Migrants’ Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Hazards and Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T08:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Ives', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c02c4d39-6efa-55f2-8f7c-0508bf1317f7', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c02c4d39-6efa-55f2-8f7c-0508bf1317f7'}, {'abstract': 'Even as she fought cancer, the singer Sharon Jones lived for the stage as a powerful, soulful presence. From legendary theaters to sweltering Midwest venues, she gave it her best.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/miss-sharon-jones-a-queen-among-dap-kings/', 'snippet': 'Even as she fought cancer, the singer Sharon Jones lived for the stage as a powerful, soulful presence. From legendary theaters to sweltering Midwest venues, she gave it her best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacob Blickenstaff has been photographing Sharon Jones and the Dap-Kings since 2009. He started out documenting shows, then recording sessions, and was eventually asked by Gabe Roth, a co-founder of Daptone Records, to shoot his first album cover for the label, “I Learned the Hard Way,” depicting Miss Jones and the group in back of their studio in Bushwick, Brooklyn. Since then, Mr. Blickenstaff has worked with the label on several other album projects. After Ms. Jones’s death last week, Mr. Blickenstaff reflected on his years with the band.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miss Sharon Jones, a Queen Among Dap-Kings', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Sharon Lafaye (1956- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dap-Kings (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T09:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Blickenstaff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blickenstaff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37d07cdb-ab0e-52a5-9cf0-57d118a4d569', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37d07cdb-ab0e-52a5-9cf0-57d118a4d569'}, {'abstract': 'Beijing’s distinct and colorful dialect is heard less and less as migration, development and language standardization programs reshape the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/world/asia/china-beijing-dialect.html', 'snippet': 'Beijing’s distinct and colorful dialect is heard less and less as migration, development and language standardization programs reshape the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — To the untutored ear, the Beijing dialect can sound like someone talking with a mouthful of marbles, inspiring numerous parodies and viral videos. Its colorful vocabulary and distinctive pronunciation have inspired traditional performance arts such as cross-talk, a form of comic dialogue, and “kuaibanr,’’ storytelling accompanied by bamboo clappers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/18/world/19CHINABEIJING-1/19CHINABEIJING-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Disappearing Dialect at the Heart of China’s Capital', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': N