 values and connect with customers who value inclusiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a new commercial for the Fisher-Price Little People Sit ‘n Stand Skyway, Lili Boglarka Havasi claps and smiles as the cars zoom down the plastic raceway. It’s a typical holiday toy ad except for one fact: Lili has Down syndrome.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-articleLarge.png', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-jumbo.png', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/10/well/family/well-family-lili/well-family-lili-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1054, 'width': 1680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Toy Ads and on the Catwalk, Models With Down Syndrome', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evoking Values, Ads Use Models With Down Syndrome', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonner, Jeanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisher-Price Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeanne Bonner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2660d419-9063-5210-aa6d-2c65fb757d8f', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2660d419-9063-5210-aa6d-2c65fb757d8f'}, {'abstract': 'A 14-year-old dying girl’s last wish is fulfilled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/learning/would-you-like-to-be-cryogenically-preserved-frozen-upon-your-death.html', 'snippet': 'A 14-year-old dying girl’s last wish is fulfilled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The saying goes that two things in life are certain: death and taxes. One of those, however, might be not so certain after all. Cryogenics is the scientific process by which a dead body is frozen in the hopes it will one day be thawed, bringing the person back to life. So far, the reversal process has happened only in movies, but that doesn’t stop some people from wanting the option.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Would You Like to Be Cryogenically Preserved (Frozen!) Upon Your Death?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf38470-e512-56e5-ae5d-2d92c7eeff80', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf38470-e512-56e5-ae5d-2d92c7eeff80'}, {'abstract': 'A confrontation with a wild black bear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/magazine/running-into-danger-on-an-alaskan-trail.html', 'snippet': 'A confrontation with a wild black bear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It happened so fast: One moment I was running trails, the next I was staring a black-bear sow in the face, so close I could smell it, wild and pungent and alarming, and I knew it could smell me, too, my fear.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/magazine/27lives/27mag-27lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/magazine/27lives/27mag-27lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 843}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/magazine/27lives/27mag-27lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'leg