rial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e142c5c7-d811-593d-850e-40d51af14c60', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e142c5c7-d811-593d-850e-40d51af14c60'}, {'abstract': 'Television’s avalanche of holiday fare began a few weeks ago on some outlets, and now it is really picking up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/arts/television/christmas-tv-programming.html', 'snippet': 'Television’s avalanche of holiday fare began a few weeks ago on some outlets, and now it is really picking up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the supposed war on Christmas is still being waged, you’d never know it from the television listings for the next few weeks. Christmas — which conservative critics have complained has been marginalized in our cross-cultural age — is everywhere this season, often right in the titles of specials and made-for-TV movies. And one of the first examples comes Friday night on that most libertine of cable outlets, HBO.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/arts/24CHRISTMASTV1/24CHRISTMASTV1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weathering a Blizzard of Christmas TV Programming', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weathering a Blizzard of Christmas Programming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T19:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a3b3399-4e9c-5951-84ba-98733bf4baf5', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a3b3399-4e9c-5951-84ba-98733bf4baf5'}, {'abstract': 'No one really pandered to them. Does that mean no one cares?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/opinion/the-farmers-we-forgot.html', 'snippet': 'No one really pandered to them. Does that mean no one cares?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One cannot rule out a blizzard in Minnesota after Labor Day, and so when I travel for Thanksgiving or any time in the fall, I am careful to fly into Des Moines instead of Minneapolis, and then drive the 200 miles north to my hometown. I like to drive through Iowa during autumn because it turns back time. When I travel straight north, I traverse latitude, moving toward a place where the thaw arrives later in the spring.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27jahren/27jahren-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 1559, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Farmers We Forgot', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Farmers We Forgot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-23T20:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Jahren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jahren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1542b79b-d263-5001-b9a8-54bdb65d6fad', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1542b79b-d263-5001-b9a8-54bdb65d6fad'}, {'abstract': 'A market debut early next year could get Snap trading ahead of anticipated stock sales by older ventures including Airbnb, Palantir, Pinterest and Uber.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/business/dealbook/snap-moving-to-ipo-faster-than-its-peers.html', 'snippet': 'A market debut early next year could get Snap trading ahead of anticipated stock sales by older ventures including Airbnb, Palantir, Pinterest and Uber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Snap wants to be sure youth is not wasted on the young. The company, which offers an app with disappearing messages and pictures, is preparing an initial public offering at the tender age of five years. That is earlier than most of its technologically minded peers, which tend to mature a little more before going public. Snap’s value, however, may yet have some growing to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption'