ession foods that did not put you in mind of Alice Waters’s ministrations in the dining halls at Yale.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/nyregion/27BIG/27BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Election? Some Students Are Too Busy to Worry', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Too Busy  to Worry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LaGuardia Community College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-24T00:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a038b87-c8a2-5073-8dc7-fdab27f69590', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a038b87-c8a2-5073-8dc7-fdab27f69590'}, {'abstract': 'Sworn statements described a scheme to cheat customers, and sales playbooks called for tapping into “the roller coaster of emotions” to get people to sign up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/23/us/would-trump-have-won-trump-university-case-evidence-says-he-faced-hard-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Sworn statements described a scheme to cheat customers, and sales playbooks called for tapping into “the roller coaster of emotions” to get people to sign up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump had repeatedly vowed he would not settle the fraud claims facing his defunct for-profit education program, Trump University. But after his election on Nov. 8, the president-elect made a surprising reversal and agreed to pay $25 million to bring the matter to a close — while claiming he would have prevailed at trial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/us/24trumpuniv/24trumpuniv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20