t the bill. But above all, you seek “The Great British Baking Show.” This is the most earnest and enjoyable of any reality-contest show in living memory, and the skills and passion on display are significant and inspiring. (“Masterclass” episodes, with Paul and Mary, are free to stream on PBS; three seasons are available for members of Thirteen and other participating PBS broadcasters.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching3/23watching3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Should Watch on Thanksgiving With a Disparate Group, Including Kids', 'kicker': 'Watch This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-24T12:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Watching', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0671286-6462-55ff-b8d1-42aec00f581b', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0671286-6462-55ff-b8d1-42aec00f581b'}, {'abstract': 'Thanksgiving often means a lot of together time. Here are some TV recommendations to please disparate tastes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/24/watching/thanksgiving-what-to-watch-with-family.html', 'snippet': 'Thanksgiving often means a lot of together time. Here are some TV recommendations to please disparate tastes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanksgiving not the time to finally watch “The Wire,” or anything too dialogue-rich: People chitchat, someone gets up to stir something — you don’t want to be shushing people or asking everyone to pause stuff while you check on the pies. It’s time for solid shows that still don’t require tremendous brainpower. Go with “Prison Break,” Fox’s big, twisty, drama answer to “Lost” from 2005. Season 1 is a solid action soap, although the show grows exhausting after that. (Netflix)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching2/23watching2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/23/watching/23watching2/23watching2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'