'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-24T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39939bf5-d377-51f3-b7fa-6a574c559361', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39939bf5-d377-51f3-b7fa-6a574c559361'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: A German submarine torpedoes the British hospital ship Britannic off the coast of the Island of Zea in the Aegean Sea, during World War I, in November 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/24/1916-pirates-sank-the-britannic/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: A German submarine torpedoes the British hospital ship Britannic off the coast of the Island of Zea in the Aegean Sea, during World War I, in November 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Despatches from Athens agree that the British hospital ship Britannic, of 50,000 tons, was torpedoed by a German submarine between eight and nine o’clock on Tuesday morning, a trifle more than two miles off the Island of Zea, while en route for Mudros, the port of Lemnos, in the Aegean Sea, where she was to take on board sick and wounded. She sank about fifty-five minutes after being struck. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/24/blogs/24oldiht-1916-britannic/24oldiht-1916-britannic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/24/blogs/24oldiht-1916-britannic/24oldiht-1916-britannic-articleLarge