 “a suit-and-tie version of the white supremacists of old, a kind of professional racist in khakis”; a recent Los Angeles Times profile ran with a photo of him in sunglasses and a black shirt, looking more like a hipster academic than a Klansman.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/25/opinion/25baker/25baker-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'White-Collar Supremacy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White-Collar Supremacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Kelly J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spencer, Richard B (1978- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ku Klux Klan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-25T08:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly J. Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e42cf103-a4d2-5bb2-b464-80f9ec5c8dc5', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e42cf103-a4d2-5bb2-b464-80f9ec5c8dc5'}, {'abstract': 'The body of a woman whose mutation keeps her on the brink of starvation may hold the secret to treating obesity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/25/opinion/sunday/the-thin-gene.html', 'snippet': 'The body of a woman whose mutation keeps her on the brink of starvation may hold the secret to treating obesity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abby Solomon suffers from a one-in-a-billion genetic syndrome: After just about an hour without food, she begins to starve. She sleeps in snatches. In her dreams she gorges on French fries. But as soon as she wakes up and nibbles a few bites, she feels full, so she ends up consuming very few calories. At 5 feet 10 inches tall, she weighs 99 pounds.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/27kennedy/27kennedy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop