?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Two people who appear to be drug addicts regularly sleep in the lobby of my rental building in East Flatbush, Brooklyn. They sneak in every afternoon behind someone who leaves the door open and stay out of the view of the cameras. The super, who lives nearby, clears them out in the morning. They are generally amiable and accommodating, but when they are high they become agitated and accost me, threatening harm  if I call the police. I am scared to report them, especially because I know they will probably be back the next day. What’s the best way to handle this?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 106, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 106}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 182, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/27/realestate/27ASK/27ASK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':