Times’s questions about the federal government’s investigation into the integrity of the Nov. 8 presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following is the full text of a statement from a senior administration official, issued to The New York Times on Friday in response to questions about the federal government’s investigation into the integrity of the Nov. 8 presidential election. The government issued the statement to The Times on the condition that it be attributable only to a senior official.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Statement on Reliability of Election Results', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-26T19:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1bac665-c7c0-5ceb-afed-febbb575cfdc', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1bac665-c7c0-5ceb-afed-febbb575cfdc'}, {'abstract': 'A detained mercenary is slowly spilling his guts on what he says were efforts to sow mayhem in the Balkans and undermine NATO.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/26/world/europe/finger-pointed-at-russians-in-alleged-coup-plot-in-montenegro.html', 'snippet': 'A detained mercenary is slowly spilling his guts on what he says were efforts to sow mayhem in the Balkans and undermine NATO.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PODGORICA, Montenegro — After multiple but unproven accusations that President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia is working hard to destabilize America’s friends in Europe, a pro-Russian mercenary detained in Montenegro is slowly spilling his guts — and providing the first insider’s account of what the authorities in this tiny Balkan nation say were Russian efforts to sow mayhem.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The 