', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48ba7b57-862d-54ab-a73d-7f0f0e5fea22', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48ba7b57-862d-54ab-a73d-7f0f0e5fea22'}, {'abstract': 'A reporter born after her family was exiled from Cuba reflects on growing up in Miami, in Fidel Castro’s shadow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/27/us/a-child-forged-in-loss-and-fury-in-a-city-far-from-havana.html', 'snippet': 'A reporter born after her family was exiled from Cuba reflects on growing up in Miami, in Fidel Castro’s shadow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — I did not meet Fidel Castro in a history book like most American children. I met him in my house surrounded by “early exile” furniture, a term my mother favored. I bumped into him at the dining room table over a meal or in the living room while the grown-ups drank tumblers of whiskey or at the beach when my mother cursed him, toes in the sand, as she remembered Cuba’s idyllic beaches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/28/us/28MIAMICUBA1-web/28MIAMICUBA1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/28/us/28MIAMICUBA1-web/28MIAMICUBA1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/28/us/28MIAMICUBA1-web/28MIAMICUBA1-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/28/us/28MIAMICUBA1-web/28MIAMICUBA1-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'lega