zpatrick’s Steady Hand Is Upended by a Late Blow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzpatrick, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T02:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/631ffac6-a724-50b0-87ed-ca894b24798d', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/631ffac6-a724-50b0-87ed-ca894b24798d'}, {'abstract': 'Success in baseball and boxing infused Cubans with a sense of pride and helped give Mr. Castro grounds to taunt and defy the United States, but also exposed financial problems and led to defections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/27/sports/under-fidel-castro-sport-symbolized-cubas-strength-and-vulnerability.html', 'snippet': 'Success in baseball and boxing infused Cubans with a sense of pride and helped give Mr. Castro grounds to taunt and defy the United States, but also exposed financial problems and led to defections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 24, 1959, months after coming to power, Fidel Castro took the mound at a baseball stadium in Havana to pitch an exhibition for a team of fellow revolutionaries known as Los Barbudos, the Bearded Ones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/28/sports/28CASTROSPORTS/28CASTROSPORTS-thumbStandard.j