h': '“I miss you,” Lawrence says over the phone to Issa toward the end of this week’s episode. This statement suggests that maybe Lawrence isn’t all that interested in the single life his friends introduce him to, full of easy sex, nights at gaudy strip clubs and a startling lack of empathy for the black women they take on as romantic partners. His phone call provides enough of a glimmer of hope to prompt Issa to leave Kelli’s birthday trip and travel home in the middle of the night. But their phone call proves to be more of a wistful goodbye than anything else, proving once again that, for all its comedic trappings, “Insecure” is far more brutal than it originally appeared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/27/watching/27insecure/27insecure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 's