rticle/c7581415-a48e-5bfa-a864-755e5c8af175'}, {'abstract': 'After almost being killed in New Jersey, a Guatemalan immigrant returned to his hometown to help provide jobs and training so people won’t have to leave.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/keeping-guatemalan-immigrants-at-home/', 'snippet': 'After almost being killed in New Jersey, a Guatemalan immigrant returned to his hometown to help provide jobs and training so people won’t have to leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a predictable narrative about immigration that assumes people would rather live in the United States than wherever they came from and that they don’t look back unless we send them back. We rarely hear about the immigrants who choose to go home voluntarily. Eduardo Jimenez is one such person. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Guatemalan Immigrants at Home', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Winokur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winokur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db8a6dc4-db2e-5517-ac04-b6e41d34a26e', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db8a