t://article/c90b09c9-2064-59f6-92ef-9d8b93a5c1b1'}, {'abstract': 'President Park Geun-hye’s government is backing away from insisting on the use of only state-issued textbooks that critics say play down darker aspects of recent history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/world/asia/south-korea-history-textbooks.html', 'snippet': 'President Park Geun-hye’s government is backing away from insisting on the use of only state-issued textbooks that critics say play down darker aspects of recent history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The South Korean government indicated on Monday that it was rolling back its plan to require schools to use only state-issued history textbooks, an apparent shift for a signature project of President Park Geun-hye as she faces a corruption scandal and an escalating public backlash.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1/29KOREATEXTBOOKS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight