National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a9280bf-cf1d-521a-a885-55ae15e0aac7', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a9280bf-cf1d-521a-a885-55ae15e0aac7'}, {'abstract': 'On a fourth-and-10 near the end of overtime, Coach Gary Kubiak could have punted or gone for it, but he opted for a 62-yard field-goal attempt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/sports/football/denver-broncos-kansas-city-chiefs-overtime-field-goal.html', 'snippet': 'On a fourth-and-10 near the end of overtime, Coach Gary Kubiak could have punted or gone for it, but he opted for a 62-yard field-goal attempt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a rollicking game drew to a close Sunday night, Coach Gary Kubiak and the Denver Broncos had a decision to make. They had the ball on fourth-and-10 at the Kansas City 44-yard line with three options: punt, go for it or try a field goal. There was just more than a minute left in overtime, and the score was tied, 27-27.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/sports/29broncos-1/29broncos-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/sports/29broncos-1/29broncos-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/sports/29broncos-1/29broncos-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',