es” newspaper is summoned by the Lord Chief Justice to state the detail of its circulation in November 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/1891-the-times-must-tell/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The London “Times” newspaper is summoned by the Lord Chief Justice to state the detail of its circulation in November 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Queen’s Bench Division today, [Nov. 28] Mr. Lumley Smith appeared in the case of Romney v. Walter and another, in support of an appeal by the defendants, the proprietors of the Times newspaper, against an order in Chambers that they should give a better answer to an interrogatory as to the circulation of their newspaper by stating approximately what the circulation was on September 25, 1891. The defendants answered that the Times had a large and extensive circulation, but could not say the exact number without a troublesome and expensive inquiry from people having no interest in the matter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1891: The ‘Times’ Must Tell', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'GREAT BRITAIN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T15:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5a5d26-a4e1-544c-afe0-56de6eb5ffcf', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5a5d26-a4e1-544c-afe0-56de6eb5ffcf'}, {'abstract': 'The televised act, performed by Tatiana Navka, a skater married to an aide of President Vladimir V. Putin, was based on the film “Life Is Beautiful.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/world/europe/holocaust-ice-dance-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The televised act, performed by Tatiana Navka, a skater married to an aide of President Vladimir V. Putin, was based on the film “Life Is Beautiful.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Dressed as concentration camp inmates, each wearing a striped uniform with the yellow Star of David sewn on, the couple glided in harmony, moving to a song from the 1997 Holocaust film “Life Is Beautiful.” Barking dogs can be heard. The routine ends with simulated machine-gun fire and the woman, looking stunned and stricken, standing alone on the ice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/europe/29russia-promo/29russia-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/29/world/europe/29russia-promo/29russia-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/europe/29russia-promo/29russia-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/europe/29russia-promo/29russia-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/world/europe/29russia-promo/29russia-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'r