/0585cecb-16a9-51b8-be45-2399b7849392'}, {'abstract': 'A man veered his car onto the sidewalk at the campus, leaped out, and stabbed several people with a butcher knife, law enforcement officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/us/active-shooter-ohio-state-university.html', 'snippet': 'A man veered his car onto the sidewalk at the campus, leaped out, and stabbed several people with a butcher knife, law enforcement officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A student at Ohio State University intentionally rammed a car into pedestrians on a busy campus sidewalk on Monday morning and then began slashing passers-by with a butcher knife, the authorities said, injuring 11 students and faculty and staff members, and setting off panic at one of the nation’s largest public universities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Is Killed in Attack at Ohio State University That Injured 11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '11 Are Injured in a Rampage at Ohio State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Adam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Artan, Abdul Razak Ali (d 2016)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horujko, Alan R (1988- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus (Ohio)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T15:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith, Richard Pérez-Peña and Adam Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d0a8f9-79d4-59db-8148-97bb61a7ceff', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d0a8f9-79d4-59db-8148-97bb61a7ceff'}, {'abstract': 'After decades of breakneck economic growth, the country’s wealth has ceased trickling down, bringing social mobility to a standstill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/opinion/stuck-at-the-bottom-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'After decades of breakneck economic growth, the country’s wealth has ceased trickling down, bringing social mobility to a standstill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — In the early 1980s, China’s top leader, Deng Xiaoping, is said to have issued his now-famous rallying cry in defense of a market economy. “Let some people get rich first,” he reportedly said, making the case that the Communist Party’s embrace of a freer market would generate new wealth that would eventually spread to all strata of society.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/opinion/29Zhang-web/29Zhang-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/opinion/29Zhang-web/29Zhang-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/opinion/29Zhang-web/29Zhang-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024,