t of parts of the city, sending thousands of people fleeing for their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/world/middleeast/aleppo-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Troops loyal to President Bashar al-Assad drove rebels out of parts of the city, sending thousands of people fleeing for their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Thousands of people were sent fleeing for their lives on Monday as rebel fighters lost a large stretch of territory to government forces in the northern Syrian city of Aleppo, in what could prove to be a turning point in the conflict, both militarily and psychologically.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/world/29Syria/29Syria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thousands Flee Aleppo, Syria, as Government Forces Advance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T16:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard and Hwaida Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/393170be-a418-5968-821e-9e6aa56f8c11', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/393170be-a418-5968-821e-9e6aa56f8c11'}, {'abstract': 'Our country’s adolescent democracy needs the support of America — and its new president, the foreign minister of Ukraine writes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/opinion/ukraine-has-made-great-progress-but-we-need-our-allies.html', 'snippet': 'Our country’s adolescent democracy needs the support of America — and its new president, the foreign minister of Ukraine writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — In the two years since the Revolution of Dignity, Ukraine has made more progress as a country than it had since declaring independence in 1991. We are finally tackling corruption in a meaningful way, and we have introduced a raft of reforms that will help the state to function better. After our economy contracted for two consecutive years, we now expect to see it grow again. And we have achieved all of this under the most challenging of circumstances: while fighting a Russian-led war that has cost thousands of lives, and with a Russian occupation of the Crimean peninsula and the Donbas region crippling our economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/27/opinion/sunday/29klimkin-inyt/29klimkin-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine Has Made Great Progress, but We Need Our Allies', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine’s path forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T16:07:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pavlo Klimkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pavlo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klimkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8d0978-1300-5df4-bab1-08c23b1f6a13', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8d0978-1300-5df4-bab1-08c23b1f6a13'}, {'abstract': 'Koen Olthuis has built more than 200 floating homes and offices, and says the concept is a solution to rising sea levels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/arts/design/offshoring-the-future-of-housing.html', 'snippet': 'Koen Olthuis has built more than 200 floating homes and offices, and says the concept is a solution to rising sea levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIJSWIJK, The Netherlands — Early next year when a converted cargo container on a floating foundation of plastic bottles opens on the flood-prone shores of Korail Bosti, Bangladesh’s largest slum, few of its users are likely to celebrate the 320-square-foot space as a revolution. Yet, according to Koen Olthuis, the lead architect on the project, it is part of the greatest transformation in urbanism since Elisha Otis built the safety brake that gave rise to the modern elevator, skyscrapers and ultimately urban density.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/arts/29Olthuis1-INYT/29Olthuis1-INYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'artic