': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T18:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4006ff7-f8b5-531d-8dfe-677f1ff2e62b', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4006ff7-f8b5-531d-8dfe-677f1ff2e62b'}, {'abstract': 'This Berkshire pork roast from a San Francisco butcher is a fragrant, delectable dish for a celebration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/dining/roliroti-porchetta.html', 'snippet': 'This Berkshire pork roast from a San Francisco butcher is a fragrant, delectable dish for a celebration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This ready-to-roast porchetta, a boneless, rolled and seasoned piece of lean pork swaddled in pork belly, comes from a third-generation butcher, Thomas Odermatt, whose RoliRoti porchetta sandwich regularly sells out at the Ferry Plaza market in San Francisco. Mr. Odermatt, whose heritage is Swiss, ships his Berkshire pork frozen. Let it thaw for a day or so in the refrigerator, and you’ll be ready to go, with a hefty roast that emerges from the oven crackling, bronzed and succulent. The stunning centerpiece is certain to impress your holiday guests, and as it cooks, it will surely perfume your kitchen like nobody’s business: RoliRoti porchetta, $150 for five to six pounds, shipped frozen, 718-389-0985, heritagefoodsusa.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30BURNER-ROAST/30BURNER-ROAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnai