e show held in October in a former train station here, heralded every sort of spirit. There was a booth pouring a new German gin. There was a stand mixing daiquiris with rum from Cuba. Nearby was a new German gin. Around the corner, a Campari bar was handing out Negronis. Further down the aisle was a new German gin.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/dining/30GIN1/30BURNER-GIN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Beer: Germany Goes All In for Gin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Of All the Gin Joints, Many Are German', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonson, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gin (Liquor)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-28T21:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd3bfc0f-82da-5e50-80b4-7ccfe94c92c2', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd3bfc0f-82da-5e50-80b4-7ccfe94c92c2'}, {'abstract': 'After the murder of Chico Mendes in 1988, a new brand of green governance developed on Brazil’s rain forest frontier, but political instability poses fresh threats.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/what-changed-and-didnt-after-the-1988-slaying-of-a-rain-forest-hero-in-brazil/', 'snippet': 'After the murder of Chico Mendes in 1988, a new brand of green governance developed on Brazil’s rain forest frontier, but political instability poses fresh threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was happy to see this fresh Retro Report production on the legacy of Chico Mendes, the Brazilian rain forest defender who was slain by a ranching family in December, 1988 as land conflicts followed road building in the depths of the Amazon. Retro Report is an innovative journalism project revisiting stories long after the headlines have flowed by. The resulting videos provide an inval