ytimes.com/2016/11/29/world/europe/chernobyl-disaster-cover.html', 'snippet': 'The shelter, under construction since 2010, covers the deteriorating steel and concrete sarcophagus hastily built after the nuclear accident 30 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Resembling an aircraft hangar, a giant arched shelter was slid into place over the Chernobyl nuclear disaster site in Ukraine on Tuesday. The shelter, the world’s largest land-based moving structure, is a feat of engineering decades in conception and years in the making.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/world/30Chernobyl/30Chernobyl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giant Arch, a Feat of Engineering, Now Covers Chernobyl Site in Ukraine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giant Protective Arch Now Covers Chernobyl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chernobyl (Ukraine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-29T17:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Nechepurenko and Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nechepurenko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0498c7fd-4158-500e-961a-202c1a7df6d7', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0498c7fd-4158-500e-961a-202c1a7df6d7'}, {'abstract': 'A pair of beloved New York restaurants opened in Palm Beach and Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/29/t-magazine/food/sant-ambroeus-smile-miami-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'A pair of beloved New York restaurants opened in Palm Beach and Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida is upping its chic quotient with the importing of two New York City institutions. Sant Ambroeus, the Italian restaurant that has outposts on the Upper East Side as well as in SoHo, the West Village and Southampton, has arrived in Palm Beach with executive chef Marco Barbisotti in tow. He’ll cook up menu mainstays such as veal in a tuna and caper sauce and saffron-flavored risotto, while also taking advantage of the town’s proximity to the sea. Meanwhile, the team behind the Smile has joined forces with the night-life impresario David Grutman and Design Miami’s Craig Robins to open OTL in the booming Design District. Sleeker than the Smile’s rustic Manhattan locations, it’s a sprawling two-story restaurant and cafe that will host events and showcase local designers — for those, Robins says, “who want a bit of culture with their coffee.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/miami/miami-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1821, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'cro