d’s largest hedge fund, of “restraining and coercing” employees from exercising their rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/29/business/dealbook/bridgewater-associates-labor-board-employee-confidentiality-contract-settlement-.html', 'snippet': 'The National Labor Relations Board had accused the firm, world’s largest hedge fund, of “restraining and coercing” employees from exercising their rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resolution of an action by the National Labor Relations Board against Bridgewater Associates, the world’s biggest hedge fund, regarding the rights of employees will remain a mystery — at least to anyone outside of the firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Settlement With Labor Board on Worker Rights Stays Secret', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bridgewater Settlement With Labor Board on Worker Rights Stays a Secret', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, Alexandra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bridgewater Associates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalio, Raymond (1949- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-29T21:31:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Goldstein and Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7902241-9d99-5431-a1dc-17bd1e53be5f', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7902241-9d99-5431-a1dc-17bd1e53be5f'}, {'abstract': 'This Brendan J. Byrne documentary gives historical context to Sands’s 1981 hunger strike and death in solidarity with the Provisional Irish Republican Army.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/29/movies/bobby-sands-66-days-review.html', 'snippet': 'This Brendan J. Byrne documentary gives historical context to Sands’s 1981 hunger strike and death in solidarity with the Provisional Irish Republican Army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a brutal war of attrition, the winning side is not the one that inflicts the most pain but the one that endures the most suffering. That concept is forcefully reiterated in Brendan J. Byrne’s documentary “Bobby Sands: 66 Days,” a stirring but impersonal political biography of Sands, a martyr to the Irish Republican Army cause who, demanding better treatment of I.R.A. inmates, refused food for 66 days and died in prison on May 5, 1981. He was 27.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30BOBBY1/30BOBBY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30BOBBY1/30BOBBY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30BOBBY1/30BOBBY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge'