tion comedown — comprises a full, chaotic schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/29/t-magazine/art/art-basel-miami-preview-guide.html', 'snippet': 'Even a comparatively subdued fair week — thanks to the Zika threat and postelection comedown — comprises a full, chaotic schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zika fears and the postelection comedown couldn’t stop the annual pilgrimage to Art Basel Miami Beach. As they say in the business, the show must go on; and in fact, that seems to be the predominant theme for this year’s Miami art week. The most dedicated attendees — exhibitors — began touching down on Sunday for the weeklong gauntlet, which runs through Dec. 4. Those collectors and visitors who scheduled early enough flights got the chance to see “Tide by Side,” a confetti-fueled parade featuring local dancers, musicians and performers who inaugurated Faena District Miami Beach, the city’s new, billion-dollar art and residential complex, on Sunday afternoon. The fanfare continued on Monday night when Faena’s ringleader, the Argentine developer Alan Faena, opened the doors of the Faena Forum, a 50,000-square-foot performance space designed by OMA/Rem Koolhaas and Shohei Shigematsu, to a crowd of V.I.P.s eager for a glimpse of its interior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/29/t-magazine/entertainment/29tmag-basel/29tmag-basel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Expect From This Year’s Art Basel Miami Beach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art Basel Miami Beach', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami Design District (Miami, Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-29T21:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kat Herriman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herriman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfaf28b5-9acb-5499-9c13-93c47bf13df1', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfaf28b5-9acb-5499-9c13-93c47bf13df1'}, {'abstract': 'Chen Gang plays a Chinese taxi driver trapped in a bureaucratic nightmare after he accidentally hits a motorcyclist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/29/movies/old-stone-review-johnny-ma.html', 'snippet': 'Chen Gang plays a Chinese taxi driver trapped in a bureaucratic nightmare after he accidentally hits a motorcyclist.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Old Stone,” a tough, bitter serving of straight-up naturalism, opens on a street and closes at the edge of the abyss. Between start and finish, it follows the nightmarish ordeals of a Chinese taxi driver, Lao Shi (Chen Gang), who struggles to do the right thing after hitting a motorcyclist. His first mistake is reporting the accident; his second is trying to help the bleeding victim instead of splitting. No good deed goes unpunished in this vision of contemporary China, a dog-eat-dog world in which the strong don’t just consume the weak, they also suck the marrow out of every last bone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30OLDSTONE/30OLDSTONE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30OLDSTONE/30OLDSTONE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30OLDSTONE/30OLDSTONE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/arts/30OLDSTONE/30OLDSTONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/art