: [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04968181-2279-5aa3-83c9-4a89999d7411', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04968181-2279-5aa3-83c9-4a89999d7411'}, {'abstract': 'The French actress consistently chooses roles that are morally complex and sometimes hard to watch. And yet we can’t bring ourselves to look away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/t-magazine/isabelle-huppert-elle-movie-interview.html', 'snippet': 'The French actress consistently chooses roles that are morally complex and sometimes hard to watch. And yet we can’t bring ourselves to look away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two unexpected orgasms in “Elle,” the latest film by Paul Verhoeven, and both are achieved by Michèle, played by the French actress Isabelle Huppert as only Isabelle Huppert could play her. Michèle is a successful, no-nonsense video-game executive, daughter of a jailed serial-killer father and a sex-obsessed cougar mother, ex-wife of a failed writer, mother to a useless son and, above all, a woman who gains mastery over her rapist by finding her own pleasure in the horrifying act. If there is another actress working today who could have pulled off this role, who could have dignified, deepened and brought humor to it, I can’t think of whom it might be.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '145', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/t-magazine/30huppert-promo/30huppert-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enduring Allure of Isabelle Huppert', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Light in the Dark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huppert, Isabelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Elle (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verhoeven, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T15:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb7c795f-b06c-5a93-9760-68b54db2bcd6', 'word_count': 1498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb7c795f-b06c-5a93-9760-68b54db2bcd6'}, {'abstract': 'This month, Petit h hosts pop-up shops at the brand’s Manhattan boutiques, where guests can join “the joy of inventing.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/t-magazine/design/hermes-boutique-holidays.html', 'snippet': 'This month, Petit h hosts pop-up shops at the brand’s Manhattan boutiques, where guests can join “the joy of inventing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pascale Mussard, the artistic director and sixth generation scion of the Hermès family, insists she “can find use for anything.” Her knack for repurposing is put to the test at Petit h, a salon des refusés of sorts, where she and her team of artisans and designers give new life to reams of raw silk, strips of crocodile skin and other extras from the Hermès ateliers. Objects range from the practical (reusable leather cupholders) to the purely playful (animal masks woven from silk scarves), but all exhibit the love of material and attention to detail for which Hermès is known. In December, Petit h will host pop-up shops at the brand’s Manhattan boutiques, complete with craft tables for guests to discover what Mussard calls “the joy of inventing.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 757}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_hermes-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crafting, the Hermès Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hermès for the Holidays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop-Up Stores and Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T15:36:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Merrell Hambleton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Merrell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hambleton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/744a538b-dd34-52ec-b9ac-6d2b0242aada', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/744a538b-dd34-52ec-b9ac-6d2b0242aada'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Young celebrates the 30th anniversary of his dance space and the inaugural choreography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/arts/bill-young-interleaving-anniversary-100-grand-street.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Young celebrates the 30th anniversary of his dance space and the inaugural choreography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago, Bill Young inaugurated a new performance space at 100 Grand Street with a program of four dances bearing the overall title of “Interleaving.” To celebrate the anniversary of that space and event, he is recreating “Interleaving” with a new cast of 14 dancers for his unusual choreographic concept. The four dances have traditional beginnings, middles and ends, but instead of a linear presentation of those sections, Mr. Young has grouped them together: All four beginnings are performed sequentially, then all four middles and, finally, all four ends. Reviewing the original production for The New York Times in 1987, Jennifer Dunning wrote that all of these forming and dissolving bits of movement were like daubs of color, making “Interleaving” resemble “an activated Jackson Pollock painting.” Any way you look at it, it’s four dances in one. (Thursday, Dec. 8, through Dec. 11, at 8:30 p.m.; 212-925-6573.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 726}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1692, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrapping 4 Dances Into 1 at 100 Grand Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Beginnings, Middles and Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Interleaving (Dance)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Bill (1954- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T15:39:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7faeabfd-c263-582d-b688-e0f0931842ce', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7faeabfd-c263-582d-b688-e0f0931842ce'}, {'abstract': 'The eccentric songwriter Justin Vernon, a.k.a. Bon Iver, has a series of 10 New York shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/arts/music/for-bon-iver-a-perfectionist-10.html', 'snippet': 'The eccentric songwriter Justin Vernon, a.k.a. Bon Iver, has a series of 10 New York shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the versatile, sometimes eccentric songwriter Justin Vernon, more fame has meant more meticulousness when it comes to how he delivers music. In the case of “22, a Million,” his third and most experimental album as Bon Iver, that attention to detail meant taking five years to finish it, as well as a carefully curated debut at his own hometown music festival, Eaux Claires, in Wisconsin.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE6/04GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE6/04GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE6/04GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE6/04GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE6/04GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 557}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 