ad_paragraph': 'It wasn’t a dream. I was standing onstage holding an Emmy. I’d imagined being in this room, clutching this statue ever since watching my first Emmy broadcast at 7 years old. Now, I was actually at the podium and accepting the award on national television. It was 2007, and I was 23. I had worked very hard to get this far, I was shooting 16-hour days to make “Ugly Betty,” and I was loving every minute of it.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 276}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA/04FIRSTTIME-FERRERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Triathlon Helped America Ferrera Defy Her Inner Critic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '… I Did a Triathlon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrera, America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triathlon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leukemia & Lymphoma Society', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By America Ferrera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'America', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferrera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/204356c7-23f4-5504-ad67-bd98fbc117de', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/204356c7-23f4-5504-ad67-bd98fbc117de'}, {'abstract': 'A prosecutor said Wednesday that Officer Brentley Vinson will not face charges in the Sept. 20 shooting of Keith Lamont Scott, whose death set off days of unrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/us/charlotte-officer-acted-lawfully-in-fatal-shooting-of-keith-scott.html', 'snippet': 'A prosecutor said Wednesday that Officer Brentley Vinson will not face charges in the Sept. 20 shooting of Keith Lamont Scott, whose death set off days of unrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RALEIGH, N.C. — There is no doubt that officers surrounded him. That they shouted at him. That they shot him. But a crucial question about the fatal confrontation between Keith L. Scott and police officers in Charlotte, N.C., has always been whether Mr. Scott was wielding a gun.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlotte Officer ‘Justified’ in Fatal Shooting of Keith Scott', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Shooting Found Justified in N. Carolina', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Keith Lamont (1973-2016)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vinson, Brentley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, R Andrew', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset and Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c7b359d-2188-54ee-ba1c-f6bbdd317cff', 'word_count': 1306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c7b359d-2188-54ee-ba1c-f6bbdd317cff'}, {'abstract': 'His lavishly kaleidoscopic productions will be shown in a retrospective starting Dec. 7.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/movies/busby-berkeleys-grand-spectacles-at-film-forum.html', 'snippet': 'His lavishly kaleidoscopic productions will be shown in a retrospective starting Dec. 7.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An ideal Hollywood moviemaker of Depression-era escapism, Busby Berkeley, the choreographer and director of musical comedies, was also a pioneer who expanded the language of cinema. Decades before C.G.I., Berkeley constructed lavishly kaleidoscopic productions: scores of dancers and musicians; elaborate sets; and innovations like revolving stages, overhead camera shots and mirrors. And generations of homage-payers have mined his giddy, surreal imagery for inspiration (Steven Spielberg in “Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom” and the Coen brothers in “The Big Lebowski,” to name but two).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/arts/04GUIDE4/04GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 873, 'width': 1174, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Busby Berkeley’s Grand Spectacles at Film Forum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film; Lavish Visuals of the ’30s and ’40s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkeley, Busby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:37:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2f1d8d3-eacf-5e12-866b-e9e618b31d3a', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2f1d8d3-eacf-5e12-866b-e9e618b31d3a'}, {'abstract': 'New cookbooks include an elaborate approach to home cooking and recipes with strong regional identities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/books/review/from-brooklyn-to-kentucky-to-iran-cookbooks-for-every-taste.html', 'snippet': 'New cookbooks include an elaborate approach to home cooking and recipes with strong regional identities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the age of internet recipes, why on earth would anyone open a cookbook? And yet we do. Printed cookbooks have been defying their own death notices for years now, probably because they don’t just offer recipes, they offer relationships. There’s a person inside those covers — someone whose voice is appealing, whose guidance is reliable and whose food evokes the world you wish you lived in. Today’s culinary celebrities may be photographed far more sumptuously than their predecessors, and their recipes may be more overtly dazzling, but their books make the same promise that once lured homemakers to Mrs. Beeton, Fannie Farmer, Betty Crocker and Julia Child. Cook like me, they’re all saying. Try this recipe, try that one. Life will be much, much better. “If you follow every step in this book, you, too, will have two children, run a start-up and live in Brooklyn,” declare Amanda Hesser and Merrill Stubbs in A NEW WAY TO DINNER: A Playbook of Recipes and Strategies for the Week Ahead (Ten Speed, $35). They’re being jovial, but they’re also evoking the dream at the heart of the cookbook business.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Cooking/1204-BKS-Cooking-jumbo.