 and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:43:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcbbde48-125b-54f9-9c07-72316fc2f05e', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcbbde48-125b-54f9-9c07-72316fc2f05e'}, {'abstract': 'Sous vide cooking is simple enough: Put a bag of food in hot water and wait. But two devices for doing this, the Joule and the Anova, differ greatly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/technology/personaltech/two-sous-vide-gadgets-face-off-in-a-kitchen-showdown.html', 'snippet': 'Sous vide cooking is simple enough: Put a bag of food in hot water and wait. But two devices for doing this, the Joule and the Anova, differ greatly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LET’S face it: Thanks to technology, we are running out of excuses for not knowing how to cook.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01TECHFIX1/01TECHFIX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01TECHFIX1/01TECHFIX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01TECHFIX1/01TECHFIX1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01TECHFIX1/01TECHFIX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 