er amid anxiety over their party’s setbacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — House Democrats on Wednesday rejected appeals that they need new leaders to win back disaffected voters, re-electing Representative Nancy Pelosi of California to an eighth term as House leader over a Rust Belt congressman who said the party had lost its connection to the American working class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nancy Pelosi Beats Back House Democratic Leadership Challenge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pelosi Rebuffs Challenge to House Leadership Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huetteman, Emmarie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Timothy J (1973- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/754f8f37-cbf1-5e45-8943-ffddcfc4f35f', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/754f8f37-cbf1-5e45-8943-ffddcfc4f35f'}, {'abstract': 'Some apps mimic a single-lens reflex camera in options and complexity, while others unleash your creativity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/technology/personaltech/take-your-smartphone-photography-to-the-next-level.html', 'snippet': 'Some apps mimic a single-lens reflex camera in options and complexity, while others unleash your creativity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH Apple’s iPhone 7 and Google’s new Pixel phones putting such an emphasis on powerful camera technology, smartphone photography is more robust than ever. And while phones typically have great built-in photography apps, many other options can be easier or expand your range.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1066, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1066}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/business/01SMART3/01SMART3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1153, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Take Your Smartphone Photography to the Next Level', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take Your Smartphone Photography to the Next Level', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iOS (Operating System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Polaroid Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa496e58-6093-595c-a788-b0640ad531e0', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa496e58-6093-595c-a788-b0640ad531e0'}, {'abstract': 'People who see sports as an escape from the real world might be surprised at just how often the two overlap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/books/review/best-new-sports-books.html', 'snippet': 'People who see sports as an escape from the real world might be surprised at just how often the two overlap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who see sports as an escape from the real world might be surprised at just how often the two overlap. The American experience constantly darts into the western Pennsylvania town of Aliquippa in S.L. Price’s PLAYING THROUGH THE WHISTLE: Steel, Football, and an American Town (Atlantic Monthly, $27). In the 1930s, Aliquippa was a site of anti-union violence, in part ended when this company town’s company, Jones & Laughlin Steel, was on the wrong side of the 1937 Supreme Court decision confirming the New Deal’s labor protections. Aliquippa rode World War II and its aftermath — “War eats steel,” Price writes in hard-boiled style — to the point where, by 1950, the United States produced nearly half the world’s steel. Aliquippa declined with the industry and struggled with racial tensions, housing discrimination, protests. In the 1980s came crack cocaine. Today, Aliquippa is a shell.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Sports/1204-BKS-Sports-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Season’s Books on Sports: A Roundup', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tracy, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:50:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50e790e5-976b-5438-a8c3-e612b6c236c4', 'word_count': 2531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50e790e5-976b-5438-a8c3-e612b6c236c4'}, {'abstract': 'The flame-ravaged Gatlinburg is a place of beauty, in a region that sorely needs it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/opinion/appalachia-burning.html', 'snippet': 'The flame-ravaged Gatlinburg is a place of beauty, in a region that sorely needs it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEREA, Ky. — My parents married in the spring of 1973, in a modest white Baptist church by a creek in a small hollow in southeastern Kentucky. My mother borrowed her sister’s wedding dress, and after the cake-and-punch reception in the fellowship hall, she changed into a baby blue minidress and set out with my father to the Smoky Mountains resort town of Gatlinburg, Tenn., for the honeymoon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01howard/01howard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Appalachia Burning', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appalachia Burning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gatlinburg (Tenn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Smoky Mountains National Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'APPALACHIAN REGION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T16:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Howard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Howard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/321413f1-aea6-5983-9143-b50b35a78af0', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/321413f1-aea6-5983-9143-b50b35a78af0'}, {'abstract': 'New books look at the careers of Brian Wilson, Paul Simon and other music stars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/books/review/rock-lives-this-seasons-pop-music-biographies-and-memoirs.html', 'snippet': 'New books look at the careers of Brian Wilson, Paul Simon and other music stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Brian Wilson was young, another kid cracked him upside the head with a lead pipe. He was rendered almost entirely deaf in his right ear. When people talked to him, he would turn his left side toward them, “like I was tuning a radio station.” And when Wilson makes music, he says, “I make mono music. I can only hear out of one side, which means that it’s already mixed down.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/1204-BKS-Music/1204-BKS-Music-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/books/r