ytimes.com/2016/11/30/world/europe/lufthansa-pilots-strike-germany.html', 'snippet': 'A strike by pilots at the airline has caused travel problems in Europe and threatened to damage Germany’s longstanding cooperation between management and labor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Lufthansa was once a proud symbol of Germany Inc., standing for the quality and smooth functionality of Europe’s No. 1 economy. But that was before the last week, when a strike by the airline’s pilots stranded more than half a million passengers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/world/01Germany1/01Germany1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lufthansa Joins Germany’s List of Companies in Distress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lufthansa, Its Pilots on Strike, Joins Germany’s List of Companies in Distress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Lufthansa AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T21:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6194eb7-31aa-55c9-a5b5-57335b19f058', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6194eb7-31aa-55c9-a5b5-57335b19f058'}, {'abstract': 'The bones of the famous fossil were pretty thick, suggesting she had a ratio of strength between her arms and legs more like a chimp than a human.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/science/lucy-bones-trees.html', 'snippet': 'The bones of the famous fossil were pretty thick, suggesting she had a ratio of strength between her arms and legs more like a chimp than a human.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lucy was a small one. She weighed about as much as the average 2nd grader and stood about three-and-a-half feet tall. But that lady (or pre-lady, because Australopithecus afarensis like her weren’t quite human) was strong. Her famous skeleton, a 3.18 million-year-old fossil also known as AL 288-1, tells us so. But to build arm bones as strong as hers, she, and possibly other members of her species, probably spent a lot of time in trees, suggests a study published Wednesday in the journal PLOS One.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1112, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1112}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 553, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/science/01TB-LUCY1/01TB-LUCY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1105, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Suggests 3.2 Million-Year-Old Lucy Spent a Lot of Time in Trees', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Branching Out: Lucy the Climber', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skeletons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australopithecines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS One (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kappelman, John W', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruff, Christopher B', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T21:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e99e7762-432b-5bb4-a945-ef54498ba9a9', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e99e7762-432b-5bb4-a945-ef54498ba9a9'}, {'abstract': 'Magical realism infuses one story collection; sex and faith underpin another. And a debut novel grabs your attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/books/books-by-clare-beams-hans-herbert-grimm-april-ayers-lawson-and-kelly-luce.html', 'snippet': 'Magical realism infuses one story collection; sex and faith underpin another. And a debut novel grabs your attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And O