oyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Childs, Lucinda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Childs, Lucinda, Dance Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T23:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/feba1ef5-06b8-52fb-9414-37cf04491ce1', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feba1ef5-06b8-52fb-9414-37cf04491ce1'}, {'abstract': 'On “Darkness and Light,” Mr. Legend treats love as something far more complex than a panacea and a fount of perpetual reassurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/arts/music/john-legend-darkness-and-light-review.html', 'snippet': 'On “Darkness and Light,” Mr. Legend treats love as something far more complex than a panacea and a fount of perpetual reassurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little darkness serves John Legend well. Without it, the love songs that regularly place him in the Top 10 — megahits like “All of Me” from 2013 — are anodyne enough to work as wedding songs; they’re a worthy and lucrative enterprise that can leave an unctuous, saccharine aftertaste. But “Darkness and Light,” his fifth studio album, treats love as something far more complex than a panacea and a fount of perpetual reassurance, with music to match.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01LEGEND1/01LEGEND1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Legend: Love Songs That Bow to Dark Shadows', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love Songs That Bow to Shadows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Legend, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Darkness and Light (Album)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T23:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizat