d', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0412bca-8ae6-59e3-96c3-8e42381f51ad', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0412bca-8ae6-59e3-96c3-8e42381f51ad'}, {'abstract': 'This lesson plan asks students to weigh potential drawbacks and advantages of the pipeline project, and then to develop a fair solution to the current standoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/learning/lesson-plans/battle-over-an-oil-pipeline-teaching-about-the-standing-rock-sioux-protests.html', 'snippet': 'This lesson plan asks students to weigh potential drawbacks and advantages of the pipeline project, and then to develop a fair solution to the current standoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several months, Native American tribes and their allies, led by the Standing Rock Sioux, have been protesting against the Dakota Access pipeline, a project that would transport oil from the Bakken oil fields in North Dakota and Montana across the Plains to Illinois. The protesters, numbering in the thousands and including members of hundreds of different tribes, argue that completing the pipeline would desecrate ancestral lands, threaten the water supply, and unfairly burden the Standing Rock Sioux tribe, which is unlikely to benefit from any economic development that accompanies the project. Energy Transfer Partners, the corporation behind the pipeline, suggests the project will lead to greater economic development and increased safety and efficiency compared to the trains that currently carry Bakken crude oil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/us/12tribes-listy9/12tribes-listy9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle Over an Oil Pipeline: Teaching About the Standing Rock Sioux Protests', 'kicker': 'Civics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T23:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'subsection_name': 'Lesson Plans', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Harris and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c89c0586-de2f-5793-90e3-2e62d7cbdac6', 'word_count': 2852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c89c0586-de2f-5793-90e3-2e62d7cbdac6'}, {'abstract': 'Announcing my annual win-a-trip contest for a student to accompany me on a reporting trip.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/win-a-trip-in-2017/', 'snippet': 'Announcing my annual win-a-trip contest for a student to accompany me on a reporting trip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m delighted to invite university students to apply for my 2017 win-a-trip contest. I’ve been holding these contests since 2006, then taking the winner along with me on a reporting trip to cover global poverty and social justice issues. My aim is to generate interest in neglected global issues with the contest, and get more people writing about these issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Win a Trip in 2017', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Global Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chad', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nicaragua', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-11-30T23:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlenam